TI  - Development of an AI-Based Academic Writing Evaluation System Using Deep Learning in EMI Contexts
AU  - Chen, Z.
AB  - The proliferation of English as the Medium of Instruction in higher education at the global level has pointed out the need for effective academic writing support systems for linguistically diverse students. This study involves the designing of an AI-based academic writing evaluation system that is targeted for use in EMI environments based upon the application of the Bidirectional Encoder Representations from Transformers (BERT) as the primary deep learning model. The system is designed to evaluate such central aspects of academic writing as the accuracy of grammar, cohesion, vocabulary richness, argumentative clarity, and use of discipline-specific words. In fine-tuning BERT on a rich collection of EMI student writings in different academic disciplines, the model is able to identify both universal and context-specific patterns of the academic discourse. The system architecture includes semantic similarity module and a task-specific classifier to produce holistic assessment and give individualized, formative feedback to the learners. This research is a part of the development of intelligent academic support technologies, and it tackles fundamental linguistic and pedagogical challenges of EMI environments. This integration of pedagogically-informed feedback, genre-awareness, and EMI-specific fine-tuning marks a novel contribution beyond conventional academic writing tools. The proposed system achieved strong results, with an accuracy of 0.92, precision of 0.90, recall of 0.91, and F1-score of 0.91 on EMI student writing datasets, demonstrating its effectiveness in real academic settings. © 2025 IEEE.
