AB  - This paper introduces a tool for auto-generating criteria-oriented feedback in higher education. A model is trained based on 39 historical student submissions and teacher ratings. The tool combines natural language processing with large language model capacities to analyze contextual criteria, for which regression trees are trained. It aims to mimic teachers when providing feedback utilizing analytic rubrics. The evaluation results with 38 new submissions reveal that predictions are good, serving as a fruitful base to optimize the process when providing formative feedback. © 2025 IEEE.
