TI  - Ada and FirstPass: Bolton College’s Digital Assistants for Students, Teachers and Campus Support Teams
AU  - Hart, J.
AU  - Hussain, A.
AB  - This chapter examines the design, development, use, governance and impact of two AI in education services at Bolton College, through the lens of two case studies; namely Ada, a campus digital assistant, and FirstPass, a formative assessment platform. Both services demonstrate how AI services can streamline processes in an educational setting. Using a critical realism perspective, the chapter delves into the social, cultural, and institutional factors influencing their design, governance, and adoption. It examines leadership and change management strategies, the collaborative and participatory approaches that were adopted, and the broader implications of AI in education services on institutional practices. The chapter highlights how these services foster operational efficiencies, improve access to information, and support teaching and learning processes while addressing the ethical and systemic considerations of AI integration in education. The narrative also reflects on how these initiatives align with the institution’s broader goals and pave the way for future Generative AI developments. The lessons learned underline the importance of co-design, distributed leadership, and stakeholder engagement in creating responsible and sustainable AI solutions. © 2026 selection and editorial matter, Geoff Baker and Lucy Caton.
