AB  - As the digital intelligence reform of accounting advances and artificial intelligence technology is widely applied in the field of accounting, the cultivation of versatile accounting talents with expertise in intelligent technologies has become a consensus in both academic and industrial circles. Correspondingly, a new formative assessment system is needed due to this reformation. Currently, the formative assessment systems in some universities are limited to individual courses. They fail to adequately consider the interconnectivity between various disciplines, and the depth and breadth of students' mastery of the professional knowledge system. To address this, teaching teams can create a knowledge map of the professional intelligent accounting knowledge system. Based on this knowledge map and combined with artificial intelligence technology, they can design a new formative assessment and feedback system. We think this system could break down barriers between courses and deepen the evaluation within professional fields. By promoting the transformation of the feedback mechanism through intelligent means, we may find a new effective way to implement the formative assessment in our newly intelligent accounting curriculum framework. © 2025 IEEE.
