TI  - Enhancing Learning Outcomes for the Dyslexic Students Using AI-Powered Assistants
AU  - Mathur, A.
AB  - One of the parameters to observe the student’s learning is assessments. Assessments are useful to check their progress. There are multiple methods for assessments like diagnostic assessment – to detect the misconceptions and to evaluating the existing knowledge; formative assessment for collecting and analyzing data on the learning of student; summative assessments – to evaluate the overall achievement of students. When a combined group of dyslexic and non-dyslexic students are in a common study platform, then the dyslexic students are usually not able to achieve the higher scores in assessments as compared with non-dyslexic students. There is a need to provide equal opportunities to such students and encourage them in higher education by offering some tailored assessments or by offering some virtual assistants. In the proposed research work, we are using artificial intelligence (AI)-powered approach that is based on assessments to find the academic learning progress in dyslexic students. Multiple AI-algorithms are used on diagnostic, formative, and summative assessments. The framework begins with the diagnosis of dyslexic students and ends with the enhanced learning outcomes. © 2025 selection and editorial matter, Thangavel Murugan, Karthikeyan Periasamy and A.M. Abirami.
