TI  - Queria: Adaptive Question Generation and Evaluation in Higher Education Using Large Language Models and Contextual Learning
AU  - Badenes-Olmedo, C.
AU  - Eyzaguirre-Barreda, P.
T2  - Scopus Preprints
AB  - This paper presents QuerIA, a system that automates the generation and evaluation of educational questionnaires in Spanish using large language models (LLMs). QuerIA integrates a simplified framework based on Bloom’s taxonomy to control cognitive difficulty, supporting both multiple-choice and open-ended question formats. Instructional documents are segmented using semantic chunking, and pedagogically aligned prompts guide the generation of question-answer pairs. The system was deployed as a publicly accessible web service and piloted at Universidad Politécnica de Madrid. During one academic semester, 341 users from 17 faculties created over 5,000 questions and provided more than 800 evaluations on clarity, alignment, and pedagogical quality. The study examines generated content, difficulty control, and user feedback. Results show that QuerIA enables scalable, adaptive, and pedagogically grounded question generation, supporting formative assessment in higher education contexts.
