TY  - CONF
TI  - Development of a Formative Assessment System for Reports Using Large Language Models and Rubrics
AU  - H. Matsukawa
AU  - C. Iwasaki
T2  - 2024 International Symposium on Educational Technology (ISET)
AB  - The formative use of rubrics has gained attention in education, particularly in first-year university report writing. This is because rubrics can clarify learning objectives, provide feedback, and promote self-regulated learning. Integration with Large Language Models (LLMs) can significantly enhance this practice. LLMs can interpret and process language-based reports and rubric criteria with high accuracy. This enables objective assessments aligned with rubric standards and offers specific advice for report improvement. These characteristics can assist in overcoming challenges associated with self-use of rubrics in independent study scenarios where feedback from teachers is unexpected or difficult to obtain. This study introduces our past practices using rubric-embedded prompts to improve students’ writing skills and presents an overview of the “Report Advisor,” a system developed using OpenAI’s GPTs platform to address technical issues, along with a brief evaluation of its feedback validity. This study presents several limitations and suggests avenues for future research in this area.
C3  - 2024 International Symposium on Educational Technology (ISET)
