TI  - Integrating ChatGPT in an Educational Platform to Provide Learning Support and Promote Critical Thinking
AU  - S. -C. Dobre
AU  - M. -A. Popescu
AU  - E. Popescu
T2  - 2025 29th International Conference on System Theory, Control and Computing (ICSTCC)
AB  - Critical thinking skills are increasingly essential in today’s rapidly evolving educational and professional landscapes. These skills enable individuals to analyze information critically, solve complex problems, and make well-easoned decisions. However, evaluating critical thinking poses significant challenges for educators due to the subjective and time-intensive nature of traditional assessment methods. Recent advances in artificial intelligence, particularly the development of large language models such as ChatGPT, provide opportunities to address these limitations. ChatGPT can facilitate discussions, offer instant feedback, and deliver personalized advice, making it a powerful tool to enhance learning experiences and improve critical thinking. Therefore, in this paper we propose EduPartnerAI, an innovative educational platform designed to integrate ChatGPT into the learning process. Students can use the assistance of the AI tool for solving their assignments and the platform provides functionalities for critically assessing the responses received and documenting the interaction. EduPartnerAI also includes mechanisms for teachers to grade assignments and analyze the students’ interaction with ChatGPT, assessing their critical thinking skills.
