TI  - WIP: Generative Artificial Intelligence in Undergraduate Software Engineering Education
AU  - J. Hemmes
AU  - R. Blumenthal
T2  - 2025 IEEE Frontiers in Education Conference (FIE)
AB  - This work-in-progress innovative practice paper presents a novel methodology to integrate generative AI in undergraduate software engineering education. This approach has been adopted in survey courses at multiple institutions and shows substantial promise in teaching software design and modeling concepts using the Unified Modeling Language (UML). Adoption of AI tools based on large language models in undergraduate courses has grown since their introduction. Despite much promise and potential, the capabilities of such tools are still limited with respect to software design. These limitations should not be seen as a hindrance to classroom use. Rather, they can be beneficial in an educational setting. Our experience suggests that augmenting design modeling activities with generative AI can improve student achievement for both in-person and online delivery formats.
