TY  - CONF
TI  - Enhancing Inquiry-Based Learning in Failure Analysis Through AI: A Case Study on Formative Assessment with OpenAI's GPT
AU  - A. Saeidi
T2  - 2025 IEEE Frontiers in Education Conference (FIE)
AB  - This innovative practice paper discusses using an artificial intelligence (AI) tool within a senior-level Failure Analysis course in materials science and engineering. Typically, failure analysis activities involve students asking investigative questions about real-world failure scenarios, but participation and frequency can be limited in traditional classroom settings. To overcome this, we developed an interactive AI expert tool using OpenAI's GPT model for formative assessment, enabling students to independently inquire, analyze case details, and determine failure causes through a structured homework assignment. The tool was evaluated by analyzing its responses for accuracy and relevance, measuring student engagement through the number and type of questions asked, and reviewing feedback from a postassignment survey. Results showed strong student engagement, with students averaging eight questions each. Although feedback indicated room for improvement in the human-like quality of AI responses, this work highlights AI's significant potential to deeply engage students and encourage higher-order cognitive skills aligned with Bloom's taxonomy.
