TI  - Exploring the Use of Machine Learning in Formative Assessment of English Speaking Skills
AU  - S. B
AU  - C. P. Krupakar
AU  - O. Baylarzada
AU  - B. Das
AU  - L. Das
AU  - P. S
T2  - 2025 International Conference on Pervasive Computational Technologies (ICPCT)
AB  - The comprehension of English speaking skills is one of the major activities of language acquisition as it gives feedback to learners. Some of the disadvantages of conventional assessment techniques such as scoring and rules base systems are non-extensibility, non-precise and immediate response rate inadequacy. Basic automated solutions of speech recognition do not reflect the sequence of speech and are not very useful in evaluating pronunciation, fluency and intonation patterns. In response to these challenges, this study presents a new CRNN model for formative assessment of speaking skills in English. The proposed CRNN utilizes CNN’s ability of capturing precise details of the spectrograms, and RNN for assessing temporal characteristics of learners’ data, allowing assessment of learning in full. The proposed method encompasses data pre-processing, feature extraction, sequence analysis and real-time formative feedback generation. Al presented experimental outcomes that support the fact that than traditional machine learning techniques, the proposed model gives higher accuracy in assessment of the key speaking skills. Moreover, using the CRNN model, students get individual immediate feedback, which contributes to the better learning. This work will help to complete the work of creating general and automatic means of language diagnostics, which will ensure the presentation of a qualitatively new level of improving the communicative competence of students in the English language.
