AU  - S. K. Tyagi
AU  - A. M. S. A. Alyammahi
T2  - 2025 International Conference on Computational Intelligence and Knowledge Economy (ICCIKE)
AB  - As higher education moves toward creating intelligent learning ecosystems, the successful integration of Artificial Intelligence (AI) depends on a deep understanding of the existing digital teaching landscape. This study provides a critical blueprint for this integration by analyzing the adoption patterns of AI-enabled interactive learning platforms among 117 faculty at a major UAE university. The analysis reveals high adoption rates for tools like Nearpod and Kahoot, which are increasingly incorporating AI for content generation and student engagement. With 57% of faculty using these platforms frequently, the findings show they are core components of the current pedagogical ecosystem. This study argues that these established usage patterns and user-validated platforms are not merely a baseline but represent the foundational layer upon which next-generation adaptive learning platforms and personalized learning systems must be built. The findings offer actionable insights for designing and implementing AI-powered educational strategies that align with demonstrated faculty behaviors and preferences.
