AB  - This research-to-practice WIP paper presents CodeInspector—an automated assessment system for CS1-level Java assignments. Designed for scalability and modularity, CodeInspector streamlines and standardizes code assessment, promoting a more equitable learning environment. Our preliminary findings suggest that CodeInspector is promising. It reduces instructors' assessment workload while providing students with immediate, formative feedback that supports an iterative learning process. Additionally, CodeInspector offers students insights into their performance through error-weighted densities benchmarked against class-wide averages.
