AU  - C. Wang
AU  - Y. Zhao
T2  - 2025 IEEE International Conference on Computation, Big-Data and Engineering (ICCBE)
AB  - The widespread adoption of generative artificial intelligence (GAI) technology is reshaping students’ learning behaviors. Therefore, we elucidated the impact of GAI on the overall effectiveness of student learning to mitigate evaluation bias in learning outcomes. We adopted a backpropagation (BP) neural network to analyze data from three consecutive undergraduate cohorts. The results showed that increased GAI usage and growing student proficiency are associated with notable improvements in learning outcomes. Specifically, higher rates of GAI adoption correlate with elevated average academic performance and reduced grade dispersion, thereby minimizing the incidence of academic failure. Sch results suggest that the integration of GAI enables students to change from routine information processing to advanced cognitive tasks such as innovation and problem-solving, enhancing learning outcomes and diminishing individual performance variability. However, since the relationship between specific GAI usage metrics and academic improvement, such as the frequency of queries, was not examined, multi-dimensional statistical validation of baseline differences among the three cohorts needs to be conducted.
