AU  - Y. Elmoataz
AU  - H. K. Aslan
AU  - I. A. Abu-Krisha
AU  - M. M. Abdelsattar
T2  - 2025 7th Novel Intelligent and Leading Emerging Sciences Conference (NILES)
AB  - Modern educational environments require unified, intelligent platforms that integrate conversational assistance, formative assessment, and secure exam management. We present Aduvia, an AI-driven system built on Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) and the Llama 3.3 large language model, which delivers subject-specific, context-aware dialogue; automated quiz generation with instant feedback. Our methodology comprises five phases: (1) content Processing via OCR and semantic chunking, (2) embedding using the e5-base-v2 model and FAISS indexing, (3) RAG-based retrieval with dynamic prompt engineering and context management, (4) generative inference on a GPU-scaled Kubernetes cluster with responsive streaming, and (5) microservices deployment with comprehensive monitoring and iterative feedback loops. Experimental evaluation demonstrates that Llama 3.3 reduces non-streaming response latency by ∼0.4 s and streaming latency by 30–40% compared to version 3.0. Embedding comparisons show that e5-base-v2 produces tighter similarity distributions (0.50–0.93) versus MiniLM (0.27–0.83). A relevance classification threshold of 0.65 yields a precision of 0.85, recall of 0.92, and F1 score of 0.88. These results validate Aduvia’s capability to enhance engagement, accuracy and operational efficiency in digital learning.
