TI  - Beyond Passive Listening: Leveraging AI and Bloom's Taxonomy to Cultivate Deeper Student Participation
AU  - L. Suryawanshi
AU  - T. Kaul
AU  - R. Sharma
AU  - P. Agarwal
T2  - 2025 International Conference on Sustainability, Innovation & Technology (ICSIT)
AB  - Conventional classroom teaching methods struggle to keep students engaged and provide real-time pedagogical feedback to the professor delivering the lecture. Our research implements an AI-driven classroom engagement model. It employs live transcription, semantic summarization, and computergraded formative assessment based on Bloom's Taxonomy. This transforms passive learning into an interactive experience. The system generates dynamic quizzes through live lecture recording and its translation into structured insights. The model is being empirically tested at NMIMS, Navi Mumbai. Our study aims to illustrate how integrating intelligent systems in classrooms can enhance student engagement and improve understanding through increased attentiveness, and it also comes with a leaderboard for students to see the ranks of their peers, which adds gamification and eventually creates a sense of competition.
