TI  - AI Educational Video Creation Methodology for University Courses
AU  - D. Tokmakov
AU  - A. Tokmakova
AU  - S. Shotarova
AU  - S. Lyubomirov
AU  - N. Mileva
AU  - K. Tokmakova
T2  - 2025 IEEE International Conference on Teaching, Assessment, and Learning for Engineering (TALE)
AB  - In response to the growing demand for scalable and engaging instructional content in higher education, this paper presents a structured methodology for Al-assisted educational video creation tailored to university-level courses. The proposed six-stage framework—spanning needs analysis, content design, AI video generation, post-production, integration, and evaluation—leverages generative AI tools to streamline production and enhance pedagogical quality. The methodology was applied in the development of a targeted micro-course on binary arithmetic, designed for the 4th-year Microprocessors and Embedded Systems course in the Information and Computer Engineering program at the University of Plovdiv. Learning management system (LMS) data identified binary arithmetic as a foundational learning barrier, prompting the creation of a modular video series using tools such as ChatGPT for scripting, ElevenLabs for voice synthesis, Sora and Runway for visual generation, and Canva Video for post-production editing. A custom virtual instructor named MIRA (Miracle Assistant) was introduced to ensure continuity and learner engagement. The resulting microlearning videos—each lasting 1-2 minutes—were embedded into the university’s LMS and aligned with defined learning objectives. This work demonstrates a scalable and pedagogically grounded approach to AI-powered video creation, offering practical guidance for educators seeking to integrate generative technologies into their teaching practices.
