AB  - One of the leading causes of back distress, spinal disorders, and musculoskeletal problems today in modern life is poor sitting posture. To address the issue, the paper develops a wearable posture-detecting belt that utilizes a gyroscope sensor and MPU6050 accelerometer for tracking sitting angles. Whenever the user’s posture crosses a certain threshold, the Arduino UNO starts processing this real-time sensor data and vibrates to alert them. Depending on the duration of deviation, the test results prove that an incorrect posture can be detected well through stepwise vibration intensity at low, medium, and high levels. It is a suitable system for home and office use because of its inexpensive price, battery-operated functioning, and comfort while wearing. The findings indicate that the system indeed encourages better sitting behavior along with minimizing the health hazards otherwise occasioned by bad postures.
