AB  - The Work-Study Diploma (WSDip) offered by Institute of Technical Education Singapore (ITE), is a unique 2.5-year apprenticeship-based programme, where ITE graduates gain a head start in their career whilst pursing a nationally recognised diploma. As it is an apprenticeship-based programme, trainees enrolled into the programme spend majority of their workweek at work, with a dedicated one day of learning at the College. Majority of the knowledge and skills learnt by the trainees are new, as the qualification caters to vertical industries such as Security Operations (WSDip in Security Operations, DPSCO). One of the challenges when learning new knowledge is uncertainty. Trainees need constant guidance and mentorship by the teacher to clarify doubts that the trainees have when comprehending new knowledge. On top of that, trainees tend to forget newly learned contents, in a matter of days, unless trainees consciously review the learned contents. According to Ebbinghaus's Forgetting Curve [1], information is lost over time if not revisited. DPSCO pilot the use of noodlefactory.ai, a unique AI teaching assistant platform that leverages the power of AI to bring automation and efficiency of learning to the trainees by being their 24/7 AI tutor. Noodlefactory.ai allows repeated practice allowing knowledge and skills retention.
