TI  - Trustworthy Artificial Intelligence-Driven Clustering Approach for Formative Feedback and Evaluation of Student Code in Computer Science Programming Commands
AU  - Y. Al Wahibi
AU  - T. Al Aidarus
AU  - S. Al Hudar
AU  - W. Al Hoqani
AU  - A. Al Salmi
T2  - 2025 IEEE International Conference on Computation, Big-Data and Engineering (ICCBE)
AB  - Scalable and fair assessment of programming assignments is challenging in higher education, particularly due to the inherently open-ended nature of coding tasks and multiple correct solutions. Traditional grading approaches rely on static answer keys or deterministic test cases, failing to capture the structural diversity. These limitations lead to inconsistencies and grading bias, imposing a significant manual burden on educators. To address these challenges, we employed unsupervised machine learning techniques, specifically clustering algorithms, to automatically group student code submissions based on syntactic and semantic similarities. The method identifies structurally comparable solutions by analyzing abstract syntax trees (ASTs), token sequences, and control-flow patterns, regardless of superficial variations in code style or variable naming. This clustering method enables batch evaluation and facilitates the application of rule-based or supervised scoring models to representative samples within each cluster, reducing grading redundancy. Furthermore, a partial credit mechanism informed by structural completeness and adherence was adopted to core logic patterns, and a feedback propagation system to ensure similar submissions receive consistent and informative commentary. These features support summative and formative assessment practices while promoting fairness and transparency. The proposed method combines the advantages of artificial intelligence with pedagogical insights, offering a scalable, accurate, and explainable alternative to manual grading. It streamlines the assessment workflow and generates valuable analytics for instructors, such as performance trends and common misconceptions. By aligning machine learning methodologies, the method contributes to the growing intelligent tutoring systems and artificial intelligence applications in education, with implications for improving equity, efficiency, and instructional effectiveness in computer science education.
