AB  - This paper describes the usage of annotation in the education field and how that will be beneficial to the students and teachers all the ways in the academics. Data annotation known to be the labelling the data it’s a process of adding the additional information to the raw data this makes the end-user readability or understanding the content easily. The aims is the use the annotation in the education filed with the different types of annotation form for example text annotation, video annotation, audio annotation, image annotation and so on. With this annotation ideology in the education field its make the data more structures and relevant for analysis and decision making, annotation is the practice of adding explanatory notes, comments, or observations to a text or piece of media in order to improve knowledge, draw attention to important points, and foster critical thinking. Data annotation benefits teachers and administrators in understanding student performance, instructional efficiency, and learning outcomes. Annotations add to the video's content by giving students additional information, explanations, or interactive aspects that improve their learning. Both traditional classroom settings and online learning environments can make use of video annotation in a number of ways. Audio annotation can be used in the educational setting to annotate a variety of audio information, including audio books, podcasts, recorded lectures, and interviews. Text annotation is a technique that can be used with a variety of text-based items, including study aids, articles, essays, and internet resources. With the help of the survey it is to be determining how employing a video annotation tool (VAT) in an online learning community affected the reflective thinking and communication skills of student teachers during practice consultations. The use of Video Annotation Software (VAS), specifically GoReact, and The purpose of the study is to evaluate how well teacher candidates' learning and growth is supported by the VAS feedback loop. Two popular platforms—Hypothes.is and Perusall—Demonstrates how these platforms can improve peer learning, formative assessment, and asynchronous learning while offering a useful framework for assessing the quality of student annotations in situations where benchmarks have not yet been established. TeamTat, a web-based text annotation tool made to effectively manage multi-user, multi-label document annotation projects, in order to address problems. Automatic image annotation (AIA), where semantic information is extracted using machine learning approaches, has become the focus of research to close this gap. Video recommendation system using different platforms.
