TI  - Research on AI Remote Terminal Personal Identity Recognition Based on reinforcement Learning
AU  - B. Yingjie
AU  - X. Zhengyuan
AU  - M. Jielun
AU  - H. Chuchu
AU  - C. Yige
T2  - 2023 IEEE 5th International Conference on Power, Intelligent Computing and Systems (ICPICS)
AB  - Due to the complexity of AI technology and the limitations of remote intelligent terminal network conditions, the process of tracking user browsing behavior on web pages can easily generate redundant data, making user identification challenging. Therefore, a reinforcement learning-based AI remote terminal user identification method is proposed. The user terminal browsing behavior is defined in the client through attributes such as user ID, accessed page address, and page title, by considering unlocking behavior, operation behavior, communication behavior, and other aspects to determine the patterns of remote terminal user behavior. The browsing information is transmitted to a central server and recorded in the terminal database to collect comprehensive user terminal data. Redundant information is eliminated using the wavelet threshold method. By continuously adjusting the reinforcement learning rewards, an AI remote terminal user behavior dataset is extracted, and the coupling relationship between user identity features and behavior features is calculated to obtain the identity identification result. Simulation results show that the proposed method can quickly and accurately identify the target user's identity, ensuring user data security and providing a more reliable AI remote operation environment.
