TI  - Design and Evaluation of Intelligent Assisted Teaching System for Building Electronic Blocks
AU  - Z. Shi
AU  - X. Xiao
AU  - D. Li
AU  - H. He
T2  - 2024 International Symposium on Digital Home (ISDH)
AB  - As a fun and educational tool, electronic building blocks have shown great potential in stimulating children's interest in e-learning and enhancing their hands-on skills. However, traditional teaching methods often rely on other people's guidance or paper tutorials, making it difficult to provide instant feedback and automated learning paths. This study describes an electronic building block assisted teaching system that uses the numerical serial number represented by a special QR code on the electronic building block puzzle as the detection object, uses a deep learning-based target detection model PP-YOLOv2 to recognize and detect its position, and the user provides feedback results. The system aims to make the process of children acquiring knowledge through blocks easier and smoother by accurately recognizing blocks and their building steps. This study verifies the usability of the system in children's education in real-world scenarios, and experimental comparisons show that the use of the system significantly improves children's hands-on skills, electrical knowledge, and creativity compared to traditional block-based learning.
