AU  - F. Li
AU  - P. Guo
AU  - Z. Liao
T2  - 2023 International Conference on Computers, Information Processing and Advanced Education (CIPAE)
AB  - Wordle is a word-guessing game that has gained popularity online. Players have to guess a five-letter word by receiving feedback in the form of colored tiles. This paper uses ARIMA and XGBoost models to solve the prediction problem covered in Wordle. The mod-el ARIMA is used to predict the number of reported results on March 1, 2023, and the predicted interval is [18986 to 21753]. After obtaining the prediction results, the paper found that the P-value of Q-statistic is 0.276 in the process of testing the model, which indicates that the prediction model is reasonable. XGBoost model in machine learning is used to predict the distribution of the reported results. Firstly, this paper conducts data processing and divide the data set into training set and a test set in a ratio of 4:1. After determining the parameters of the XGBoost Model, the paper uses the test set for Supervised Learning, obtaining the prediction results of the distribution. The values of MSE, MAE and RMSE are all between 0 and 0.1, and it is concluded that its prediction ability is strong. In addition, the paper evaluates the sensitivity of each model, perturbs the relevant parameters in the range of 5%, and find that the dependent variable changed significantly, which means good sensitivity of the model.
