TI  - Enhancing Efl Senior High School Students’ Vocabulary Acquisition Using Quizlet Flashcards
AU  - S. Saputra
AU  - M. H. Mohd Tahir
T2  - 2025 11th International Conference on Education and Technology (ICET)
AB  - This study investigated the impact of Quizlet Flashcards (QFs) on vocabulary acquisition among tenth-grade students in senior high schools in Banda Aceh, Indonesia. A quasi-experimental one-group pretest-post-test design was employed to examine students’ vocabulary learning outcomes. Thirty participants engaged in a 12-week intervention (24 sessions) using QFs features such as Match, Learn, Spell, and Test, with target words aligned to the Indonesian K-13 curriculum. Data were collected through pre- and post-tests as well as a student feedback questionnaire. In addition to descriptive statistics, inferential analysis revealed significant improvement from pre-test (M= 62.5, SD= 8.38) to post-test (M= 93.83, SD= 4.68), t (29= 17.41, p<.001, with a large effect size (Cohen’s d= 3.18). Students also reported highly positive perceptions of QFs as a digital learning tool (M= 4.48, SD= 0.59). The findings highlight the pedagogical value of QFs, supported by Dual Coding Theory, Multimedia Learning Theory, and Cognitive Load Theory, in enhancing vocabulary retention through multimodal learning. While the study demonstrates strong short-term gains, limitations regarding sample size, lack of control group, and generalisability are acknowledge. Practical implications for teachers and directions for future research are discussed.
