AU  - Galit Shmueli
T2  - Information Quality: The Potential of Data and Analytics to Generate Knowledge
AB  - This chapter introduces the application of the InfoQ framework to education‐related studies. It includes four case studies. The first is the Missouri Assessment Program report card. Two other case studies are related to the application of value‐added models (VAMs) in education. One study looks at the impact of value‐added teachers on students’ long‐term gains. The other uses VAM to determine career paths and compensation of teachers in US schools. The fourth case study is about the application of conceptual understanding methods to assess student deep learning outcomes. Our first analysis is of an empirical study. The second is of a cautionary statement issued by the American Statistical Association (ASA) regarding application of VAM. With these examples, we show how the InfoQ framework can be used to analyze both an empirical study as reported in an academic paper and a statement by an organization. The final case study presents an approach used for assessing conceptual understanding, as opposed to memorization and technical task capabilities.
