AU  - DeLuca, Christopher
AU  - Barnes, Nicole
AU  - Birenbaum, Menucha
AU  - Kimber, Megan
AU  - Koch, Martha
AU  - Looney, Anne
AU  - Poskitt, Jenny
AU  - Smith, Kari
AU  - Wyatt-Smith, Claire
T2  - Policy futures in education
AB  - This paper discusses the evolution of assessment for learning (AfL) across the globe with particular attention given to Western educational jurisdictions.  Scholars from Australia, Canada, Ireland, Israel, New Zealand, Norway, and the  United States discuss prominent assessment reforms within their respective  countries over the last decade. Particular attention is given to the impact of  the pandemic as well as technological developments for classroom assessment  policies and practices. Ongoing tensions that exist between AfL and summative  forms of assessment within national policy initiatives are also revisited in  relation to the seminal version of this article published 10 years ago.
