TI  - A Hybrid Parrot Optimization Algorithm for Engineering Application and Academic Performance Prediction
AU  - Yang, Z.
T2  - Engineering Letters
AB  - Parrot optimization is a newly proposed metaheuristic algorithm in recent years, but it also suffers from the problems of easy to fall into local optimum, as well as convergence accuracy is not fast enough, in order to improve the efficiency of parrot optimization as well as solving ability, this paper proposes a hybrid parrot optimization algorithm, called PO-SCA. First, in order to solve the above defects of parrot optimization, we integrate the sine-cosine algorithm, and the two algorithms can complement each other’s advantages. Next, we verified the performance of PO-SCA on the CEC 2022 test set, and PO-SCA achieved better performance compared to the other three classical algorithms. Last, in order to validate the solution capability of hybrid parrot optimization, we used it to solve two real-world engineering cases and optimize the parameters of BP neural networks, validated it on a real dataset of college students’ academic performance prediction. The experimental results demonstrate that the proposed algorithm exhibits remarkable competitiveness in classic test sets and realworld application case. © 2026, International Association of Engineers. All rights reserved.
