AB  - In order to achieve SDG 4, which promotes inclusive and high-quality education, smart technologies are essential. In order to ensure equal learning opportunities, Smart Technologies for Achieving Quality Education: Towards Sustainable Development Goals examines how these innovations close disparities in quality and access. The book looks at how digital tools like data analytics, blockchain, AI, virtual reality, and adaptive learning systems are changing education. The introduction emphasizes how vital it is to update teaching strategies for the digital era and give students the necessary tools. Smart technologies optimize teaching methods, improve engagement, and personalize instruction. Blockchain guarantees safe credential verification, AI offers tailored feedback, and digital platforms facilitate flexible learning. All these resources work together to create inclusive classrooms that assist students from a variety of socioeconomic backgrounds. But issues like the digital divide, privacy issues with data, and moral conundrums need to be resolved. Careful preparation is required to bridge the gap between privacy protections and technology access. For AI-driven decisions to be implemented ethically, fairness is essential. The book includes case studies that show how smart technologies enhance academic performance, collaborative learning, and student involvement. To sum up, the first chapter exhorts educators and legislators to use smart technologies to promote educational equity. It demands thoughtful integration to guarantee equity, inclusion, and moral application. Education may become more transformative and accessible by carefully integrating these advances, supporting sustainable development and SDG 4. The chapter lays the groundwork for a more thorough examination of how technology will influence education in the future. © 2026 A. Jose Anand and Saravanan Krishnan.
