TI  - Computer Science-Integrated AI Education in K-12: Implementation Status and Challenges for IT Educators
AU  - Lin, J.
AB  - With the advent of the artificial intelligence era, educational models and teaching practices are facing unprecedented challenges, especially for information technology (IT) teachers in primary and secondary schools. In this context, it is particularly important to implement artificial intelligence (AI) education that integrates computer science (CS). Previous studies have mainly focused on the design of AI curriculum frameworks, but there is still relatively insufficient exploration of the implementation of frontline IT teachers in actual teaching. Based on this, this study adopts a mixed research method combining quantitative surveys and qualitative interviews to systematically examine the implementation level of K-12 IT teachers in CS integrated AI education. The research results indicate that teachers mainly face four major challenges in teaching practice: lack of a sound teaching paradigm, insufficient integration of ethical education, uncontrollable risks in the normalization of AI teaching, and inconsistent teaching directions. These findings have significant implications for future policy-making, teacher professional development, and the effective implementation of AI education in computer science courses. © 2025 Copyright held by the owner/author(s).
