TI  - AI Technology Empowering Teaching Innovation in Civil Engineering at Local Universities: Practical Exploration in the Concrete Structure Design Course
AU  - Zhang, C.
AU  - Wang, X.
AU  - Zhou, C.
AB  - This paper addresses issues such as rigid teaching modes and singular evaluation systems in the teaching of Concrete Structure Design for civil engineering majors in local universities, exploring pathways for deep integration of artificial intelligence (AI) technology with course teaching. The study took 59 students from grade 2022 of civil engineering major at a local university as the research object, conducted a 17-week teaching practice, and compared their learning performance with 66 students from grade 2021. An interdisciplinary knowledge graph containing 14 core knowledge nodes was constructed. Based on AI technology, personalized learning was realized through the analysis of students' learning behaviors such as online learning time, homework completion, and in-class exercises. A closed-loop evaluation system consisting of "process-oriented assessment (40%, including regular homework, in-class exercises, completion of task points, autonomous learning, etc.) + outcome-oriented assessment (60%, knowledge point coverage ≥ 90%)"was established, forming a complete AI-empowered teaching model of "resources-teaching-evaluation". Practice shows that this model significantly enhances students' knowledge application capabilities (average score of the experimental group is 72.2, while that of the control group is 68.6; the rate of first class performance increases from 10.2% to 23.7%) and learning enthusiasm (with an average online learning duration reaching 8.6 hours). This study provides a replicable practical paradigm for the digital transformation of engineering courses in local universities. © 2025 Copyright held by the owner/author(s).
