TY  - JOUR
TI  - A systematic and bibliometric review of artificial intelligence in sustainable education: Current trends and future research directions
AU  - Abulibdeh, A.
T2  - Sustainable Futures
AB  - This study aims to comprehensively analyze the use of Artificial Intelligence in Education (AIED), encompassing its applications, challenges, gaps in research, and future research directions. The research involves examining a wide range of studies published over the last five years and categorizing the literature into nine distinct categories, which are connections to existing educational theories, AI in Early and K-12 education, AI and ethics in education, AI techniques and applications, Artificial Intelligence (AI) and sustainable education, AI in higher education, AI in language and English as a Foreign Language (EFL) education, AI and Large Language Models (LLM), and AI in specific educational fields. The findings reveal significant trends, including the increasing integration of AI in personalized learning, ethical concerns, and the necessity for AI literacy among educators and students. The study also underscores gaps in current research, particularly in the areas of ethical implications and the scalability of AI solutions. The results suggest that while AI has the potential to enhance educational practices, further research is crucial to address the challenges and ensure the ethical and equitable implementation of AIED. © 2025 The Author(s)
