AB  - We explore the integration of AI and nanotechnology in STEM education, highlighting their potential to transform pedagogical approaches and prepare students for future technological progress. The chapter underscores the importance of embedding AI and nanotechnology into STEM curricula by reviewing recent scientific literature. It explores how AI can enhance teaching practices, assessment methods, and ad-ministrative tasks, thereby offering personalized learning experiences that boost student engagement and performance. Furthermore, the chapter highlights how nanotechnology can bridge the gap between theoretical knowledge and practical application, providing students with hands-on experience using advanced materials and techniques. An analysis is provided of the curriculum development frameworks, effective integration strategies, and the challenges and solutions related to implementing these technologies in education. A sizable section is dedicated to a case study at the University of Bucharest, Faculty of Physics, where AI and nanotechnology have been successfully incorporated into STEM programs, demonstrating their impact on students' skillsets. No part of this publication may be reproduced, stored or distributed in any form or by any means, electronic or mechanical, including photocopying, without written permission from the publisher. Use of this publication to train generative artificial intelligence (AI) technologies is expressly prohibited. The publisher reserves all rights to license its use for generative AI training and machine learning model development. © 2026 by IGI Global Scientific Publishing. All rights reserved.
