AU  - Lebese, T.
AB  - This chapter provides a bibliographic review regarding the adoption of Artificial Intelligence (AI) in accounting and audit education for the years 2014 to 2024. Using 21 peer-reviewed articles from the Dimensions database, the study examines trends in temporal publication activity, thematic emphasis, geographic authorship distribution, and AI-related teaching innovations. The results show that from 2022 to 2024, there was a substantial increase in attention from scholars, with South Africa, the United States, and Qatar emerging as key contributors. The chapter concludes with an overview of the AI-related pedagogical research gaps identified, along with strategic recommendations concerning curriculum design, faculty policy development, and inclusive governing policies. The chapter aims to support educators and policymakers looking to transform accounting education in the context of contemporary technological advancements. © 2026, IGI Global Scientific Publishing. All rights reserved.
