AU  - Suwandi, S.
AU  - Yamtinah, S.
AU  - Sarwanto, n.
AU  - Ciptorukmi, A.S.
T2  - AIP Conference Proceedings
AB  - Entering the era of artificial intelligence (AI) dominance, stakeholders in the field of education are required to adapt and align themselves with technological advancements. Educational stakeholders need to evaluate the potential of AI as a support tool in mathematics education by analyzing its performance in providing solutions to given problems. Therefore, a study on the analysis of the quality of answers generated by ChatGPT has become highly necessary. This research aims to analyze the utilization of ChatGPT in solving mathematical problems, with polynomial problems selected as the object of analysis. The method used in this study is content analysis, with polynomial problems sampled from various subtopics using purposive sampling. The data analysis technique employed in this research is the Exact Match method, which is used to evaluate the answers generated by ChatGPT in solving polynomial problems and to measure its effectiveness. The results show that ChatGPT performs well in polynomial topics, as indicated by a significant degree of similarity and a high percentage of correct answers. While ChatGPT can address basic problems effectively, it still requires further development for more complex tasks or advanced logical reasoning. The implications of this study highlight the need for educators and students to understand that ChatGPT serves as a supporting tool, not as a guide, and therefore, a prudent approach in its use is necessary. © 2025 Author(s).
