AB  - As artificial intelligence becomes more prevalent and widespread in the field of education and teaching, its applications in personalized learning, intelligent assessment, adaptive teaching, virtual assistants, and other areas are becoming increasingly extensive. AI holds great potential and prospects for development in education, but it also faces a series of challenges. This paper aims to provide a systematic review of recent research on AI-assisted teaching. By comprehensively analyzing recent relevant papers, we explore its applications and the challenges it faces. We find that although AI technologies, such as generative models, demonstrate significant potential, there are still issues such as data privacy and algorithmic bias that need further improvement. © 2025 Copyright held by the owner/author(s).
