AB  - The advent of Artificial Intelligence (AI), specifically Generative AI (GenAI), has had a profound impact on various sectors, including education. As AI technologies rapidly evolve, educational management must adapt to these shifts by rethinking traditional policies and embracing new paradigms. This paper explores how AI-supported education policies can transform the governance, decision-making and strategic planning processes in educational institutions. By analysing the implications of AI on education management, the study provides a comprehensive framework for navigating the challenges and opportunities brought about by this technological revolution. © 2026, IGI Global Scientific Publishing. All rights reserved.
