TI  - Classroom Behavior Identification and Analysis based on ResNet-50 and YOLOv5
AU  - Guo, X.
AU  - Wang, Z.
AU  - Sun, X.
AU  - Dong, P.
AU  - Tseng, S.-P.
AU  - Yang, Y.
AB  - With the development of artificial intelligence technology, deep learning models are more and more widely used in the field of behavior recognition. After careful annotation and in-depth training of a large number of classroom videos, this study has successfully constructed a dataset covering students’ multiple classroom behaviors. The YOLOv5 algorithm was used to detect the human targets in the dataset, and feature extraction with ResNet-50 was carried out, thus presenting an efficient and accurate classroom behavior identification method. This method not only improves the identification accuracy, but also improves the identification efficiency. The classroom can be organized in real time to accurately identify students’ behaviors, including listening, playing with mobile phones, discussing, sleeping, reading, walking, etc., so as to provide comprehensive classroom feedback for teachers. By analyzing these behavioral data, teachers can better understand students’ learning status, optimize teaching strategies, and improve teaching quality. Moreover, the method can be applied to other scenarios, such as conference rooms, libraries, to provide reference for behavior analysis research. For the comparative effect, four data sets were used in this study, increasing number of images for each dataset, the maximum number of images is 946, and the best effect; and Convolutional Neural Networks (CNN), ResNet-50 and ResNet-50 with Dropout were used for model comparison experiments, where the accuracy of the CNN was 0.892, the experimental accuracy of ResNet-50 was 0.925, the accuracy of ResNet-50 with Dropout was 0.919. The experimental results show that the best accuracy and the best performance based on ResNet-50 and YOLOv5 algorithms. © 2024 Copyright held by the owner/author(s).
