AB  - This chapter explores the role of technology in shaping online learning communities within higher education. Drawing on findings from a faculty survey and recent innovations, the chapter examines how tools such as learning management systems, adaptive platforms, and AI-powered technologies are enhancing student engagement, personalization, and accessibility. It also addresses critical challenges including digital equity, academic integrity, and pedagogical alignment. Emphasis is placed on the intentional integration of technology to support inclusive, student-centered learning environments. The chapter highlights strategies for effective implementation, ethical considerations surrounding emerging technologies, and the importance of maintaining educational objectives as central to technological adoption. By analyzing current trends and anticipating future innovations, this chapter provides a comprehensive framework for educators, administrators, and policymakers to harness technology's potential while upholding the integrity and humanity of the educational experience. © 2026, IGI Global Scientific Publishing. All rights reserved.
