AB  - This chapter explores how a standalone AI-powered chatbot supported student learning in a 15-week Marketplace Simulations business course. Thirty-six undergraduates used the chatbot (built on React.js-Node.js with RAG and fine-tuned models) for adaptive assistance during high-intensity decision rounds. Mixed-methods analysis (logs, surveys, focus groups) showed reduced anxiety, increased self-efficacy, and improved performance. Cluster analysis revealed strategic users benefited most from iterative interactions. Despite technical constraints, manual credential synchronization and knowledge updates proved effective. The study demonstrates conversational AI's potential as flexible, impactful support in simulation-based learning, balancing generative capabilities with structured pedagogical grounding. © 2026, IGI Global Scientific Publishing. All rights reserved.
