TI  - Mental load, ChatGPT, and work-study balance: A TAM-based study of AI adoption by employees in non-traditional education
AU  - Bashir, H.
AU  - Zhou, R.
T2  - Telematics and Informatics Reports
AB  - The study explores using an AI-driven learning tool, particularly ChatGPT, to assist employees enrolled in distance learning and weekend programs. As AI tools have been embedded in education, limited research has explored their effectiveness in non-traditional educational settings. Despite the advancement of AI-driven technologies in education, few studies have been conducted on their efficacy in non-traditional educational environments. This study investigates how employees who face mental load due to balancing work and Study utilise ChatGPT to complete academic tasks. Data was gathered from 302 employees participating in various programs at universities in Pakistan, using a quantitative study design. The study revealed that employees facing a significant mental load from work-related tasks are more likely to use ChatGPT as an assistive tool for academic assignments. The findings also demonstrate that positive assessments of ChatGPT's benefits promote behavioral intention and actual usage, highlighting its potential to enhance work-study balance. The study revealed findings with significant consequences for educational institutions and policymakers. Integrating AI tools like ChatGPT into effective educational programs helps address the specific requirements of employees. The study also provides suggestions for optimal technology use and enhances the current knowledge on the pedagogical consequences of artificial intelligence tools in adaptable education environments. © 2025
