AB  - This chapter presents a bibliometric analysis of research on artificial intelligence (AI) in youth and family contexts, based on 460 Scopus-indexed publications from 1993 to 2025. Utilizing tools such as BiblioMagika®, OpenRefine, VOSviewer, and Biblioshiny, it maps the global knowledge structure, publication trends, thematic developments, and key contributors. Results show rapid growth in recent years, with the United States leading in output and collaboration. Major themes include youth mental health interventions, human-robot interaction, and ethical concerns. The field spans computer science, social sciences, and medicine, reflecting its interdisciplinary nature. However, gaps remain in systematic reviews, cross-cultural research, longterm impact evaluations, and user-centered design. The chapter highlights the need for more integrated, collaborative, and ethically grounded research approaches to support the responsible application of AI in youth and family settings. © 2026, IGI Global Scientific Publishing.
