TI  - Analyzing Artificial Intelligence Utilization in Foreign Language Education in Higher Education
AU  - Ülker, U.
AB  - This study systematically reviews 44 Web of Science- indexed articles to examine the integration of artificial intelligence (AI) in foreign language education within higher education. Findings indicate that AI implementation in this field is a recent trend, with research activity increasing notably since 2022, especially in countries such as People's Republic of China and Ukraine. Key areas explored include teacher competence, ethical implications, AI tools for feedback, and assessment practices. AI demonstrates strong potential in enhancing language skills, particularly writing, speaking, vocabulary, and grammar. Despite its growing presence, AI research in this domain remains limited. The review identifies the need for greater collaboration, professional development, and ethical considerations. Furthermore, the study aligns with Sustainable Development Goal 4, underscoring AI's capacity to support inclusive and quality education. © 2026, IGI Global Scientific Publishing. All rights reserved.
