TI  - The Role of Artificial Intelligence in the Development of Learning and Social Innovation Education for Entrepreneurs in Poverty: A Sustainable Entrepreneurial Approach
AU  - Salamzadeh, A.
AU  - Hadizadeh, M.
AU  - Zanjireh, A.M.
AU  - Yasin, N.
AU  - Ghafelebashi, S.F.
AB  - Artificial intelligence (AI) is revolutionizing education, creating exciting opportunities and challenges. This study explores the impact of AI on education and learning as a driver of social innovation, focusing on Iran and Turkey. The field of Artificial Intelligence in Education (AIED) has seen significant growth thanks to advancements in computing and data processing. AI applications in education offer new capabilities, enhancing educational practices and promoting social innovation. This research examines how AI technologies, such as machine learning (ML) and data analysis, can improve educational processes and empower individuals. We conducted a comparative analysis of Iran and Turkey, examining their approaches to leveraging AI for educational advancement and social innovation. Our study employs a mixed-method approach, combining the fuzzy Delphi method (gathering expert opinions on key factors) and the MARCOS method (ranking those factors based on importance and uncertainty). Our findings reveal significant differences in AI adoption between the two countries. Iran faces infrastructural limitations and resource constraints, that hinder its ability to fully unlock AI's potential in education. In contrast, Turkey's robust infrastructure and proactive government policies have facilitated significant progress in AI integration, leading to the development of smart learning platforms and AI-based assessment tools. This study emphasizes the crucial role of government support, educational programs, and fostering innovation ecosystems in advancing AI-based education. Responsible AI deployment necessitates careful consideration of ethical implications and a commitment to ensuring social inclusion. This research provides valuable insights for policymakers and educators in both countries. By strategically planning and implementing AI initiatives, they can enhance educational outcomes and promote social innovation. Ultimately, this study offers a comprehensive analysis of AI's impact on education in Iran and Turkey. By identifying and ranking key drivers of AI integration, we provide a nuanced understanding of how AI can effectively enhance education and empower individuals. This knowledge contributes to the ongoing conversation on AI in education and its role in fostering social progress. © 2025 Nova Science Publishers, Inc. All rights reserved.
