TI  - Developing Digital Citizenship Skills
AU  - Subrahmanyam, S.
AB  - In the era of Society 5.0, where technology increasingly shapes society, developing digital citizenship skills has become essential. This chapter explores the integration of artificial intelligence (AI) into curriculum innovation to foster digital citizenship, emphasizing the need for ethical, responsible, and effective participation in the digital realm. It defines digital citizenship as a blend of technical proficiency and ethical responsibility, discussing AI's role in personalized learning and content delivery. The chapter presents a framework for developing core competencies like digital ethics, privacy, and critical thinking, while addressing challenges such as misinformation and unequal access to technology. It advocates for AI-driven approaches, including gamification and simulation, to enhance learning and offers strategies for embedding digital citizenship across educational curricula to prepare individuals for the complexities of Society 5.0. © 2026 by IGI Global Scientific Publishing. All rights reserved.
