TI  - Promoting Artificial Intelligence in UAE's Teacher Education: Global Insights on Ethics, Policies, and Emerging Practices
AU  - Massouti, A.
AB  - This chapter examines contemporary issues of integrating Artificial Intelligence (AI) in teacher education within global contexts, addressing concerns surrounding ethics, policies and emerging practices. Further, the chapter seeks to promote AIintegrated teacher education programs in the United Arab Emirates (UAE) through an exploration of local and international perspectives that support teacher education preparation for AI-integrated classroom practices. Moreover, the chapter examines how AI can contribute to personalized learning and teaching methodologies adopted by future teachers, as well as the advancement of sociocultural dynamics and collaboration in the classroom. Ultimately, this chapter constitutes a timely addition to the ongoing discourses on AI use in teacher education, offering new insights to current and future educators, policymakers, and researchers of teacher education and policies in the UAE and beyond. © 2026 by IGI Global Scientific Publishing. All rights reserved.
