TI  - Integrating Artificial Intelligence and Technology Into UAE Teacher Licensing Systems for Global Education Reforms
AU  - Abdallah, R.K.
AU  - Awad, M.J.
AB  - This chapter examines the integration of Artificial Intelligence (AI) and advanced technology into the UAE teacher licensing system, positioning it within the context of global education reforms. It explores the current challenges of the UAE's teacher licensure framework, including scalability, fairness, and alignment with modern educational standards. The chapter highlights the transformative potential of AI tools, such as adaptive testing, predictive analytics, and blockchain-based credentialing, in creating a streamlined, equitable, and inclusive licensing process. By analyzing UAE-based initiatives and global best practices, it provides actionable recommendations for policymakers to establish a future-ready, technology-driven teacher licensing system that supports the nation's education reform goals. Ethical considerations, such as data privacy and inclusivity, are also addressed to ensure responsible adoption. This chapter contributes to the discourse on how the UAE can lead in integrating AI into education while maintaining cultural and policy alignment with global standards. © 2026 by IGI Global Scientific Publishing. All rights reserved.
