TI  - Using AI for curriculum development and content generation: Enhancing diversity, inclusion, and adaptability in language education
AU  - Rouabhia, R.
AB  - This chapter discusses the role of artificial intelligence in transforming curriculum development and content creation for language education. In fact, with institutions of learning under increased pressure to ensure that learners have more personalized, inclusive, and culturally sensitive learning experiences, AI emerges as a powerful tool in addressing such demands. The chapter examines how AI technologies enable adaptive learning pathways, in-class real-time feedback systems, and support for diverse learning styles using multimodal content delivery. It is intended to further examine such implementation of the use of AI-driven solutions for developing culturally responsive materials while maintaining the highest pedagogical standards. Discussions will involve key areas: personalization strategies, frameworks for the inclusivity of cultures, accommodation in terms of learning styles, and analytics for continuous improvement in real time. © 2025, IGI Global Scientific Publishing.
