AU  - Al-Romeedy, B.S.
AU  - Hussein, H.
AU  - Emam, M.
AU  - Singh, A.
AB  - The integration of Artificial Intelligence (AI) and the Metaverse has revolutionized modern scientific research, offering unprecedented opportunities for innovation while presenting significant challenges. This study explores the dual nature of these technologies, focusing on their potential to transform research methodologies, foster interdisciplinary collaboration, and enable immersive experimentation. AI's capabilities in data analysis, simulations, and hypothesis generation, coupled with the Metaverse's immersive environments, have opened new frontiers in fields such as healthcare, climate science, and education. However, these advancements raise critical ethical concerns, including data privacy, algorithmic bias, and digital well- being, as well as security risks such as data breaches and misuse of AI- generated outputs. Additionally, the study examines the impact of these technologies on research dynamics, emphasizing their role in enhancing global collaboration and accelerating scientific discovery, while highlighting risks of digital exclusion and over-reliance. © 2025, IGI Global Scientific Publishing. All rights reserved.
