TI  - ChatGPT-4: A Fresh Lens on Holistic Education's Reimagination
AU  - Baskara, F.X.
T2  - AIP Conference Proceedings
AB  - The traditional boundaries of education undergo constant reconsideration as technology, especially artificial intelligence (AI), gains increasing importance in modern pedagogy. A remarkable AI model, ChatGPT-4, remains at the heart of this scholarly enquiry. The core of the investigation revolves around the pivotal question: How can ChatGPT-4 aid in constructing a more holistic, constructive education system? Prevailing research reveals promising links between AI and active, constructivist learning paradigms. However, the potential of AI, particularly ChatGPT-4, in fostering all-encompassing education merits deeper exploration. This study brings this emerging topic under the scholarly spotlight, reinforcing its relevance in the face of traditional teaching limitations and emphasising the necessity for innovation in education. Navigating uncharted waters, this research adopts an analytical approach to dissect ChatGPT-4's application within a constructivist framework. The examination probes its function as an active learning facilitator and personalisation tool, offering a novel perspective on enhancing cognitive, affective, and psychomotor domains. Findings underscore ChatGPT-4's transformative potential in broadening learning experiences, nurturing critical thinking skills, and accommodating individual learners' needs. Delving into the ramifications of these discoveries, it becomes evident that embracing AI and tools like ChatGPT-4 can stimulate the metamorphosis of learning paradigms. This fresh perspective fills a gap in previous research, revealing pathways to actualising AI's contribution to holistic education. © 2025 American Institute of Physics Inc.. All rights reserved.
