TI  - Beyond AI-enabled classrooms: Fostering critical thinking in the age of generative artificial intelligence
AU  - El Samaty, M.
AB  - Generative Artificial Intelligence (GenAI) has revolutionized various sectors, and education is no exception. The emergence of AI provided exciting opportunities for educators to enhance classroom instruction and enrich students' learning experiences and engagement. However, concerns exist regarding the potential impact of AI on students' critical thinking, a crucial 21st-century skill. This chapter explores the role of AI in learning, examining both the opportunities and challenges associated with its integration in education. It highlights the importance of fostering higher order thinking skills in school students, using the lens of Freire's critical pedagogy. By leveraging the SAMR (Substitution, Augmentation, Modification, Redefinition) Model, the chapter equips K-12 educators with practical guidance and examples to effectively foster school students' critical thinking abilities while using AI, thus empowering them to become discerning learners. Finally, the chapter discusses the implications for teacher education programs in preparing educators for the GenAI landscape. © 2025, IGI Global Scientific Publishing. All rights reserved.
