AB  - This paper critically analyses the contributions of smart education to lifelong learning. It begins by addressing the complexity of knowledge in times characterised by Volatility, Uncertainty, Complexity, and Ambiguity (VUCA) from the perspective of learning ecologies. This approach establishes a foundation to emphasise the importance of developing resilient capacities in the new digital era, which necessitates the transformation of pedagogical strategies through smart education. While tools have emerged that can integrate certain sectors of the population and enhance the speed of information management, challenges persist that demand critical thinking for more effective utilisation of personal and technological resources. The paper concludes that educational systems must undergo transformation, not only by empowering the potential of educational actors through intelligent spaces but also by fostering awareness of future educational challenges and opportunities. © 2025, IGI Global Scientific Publishing. All rights reserved.
