AU  - Evkaya, O.
AU  - Genc, O.
AB  - In the last couple of decades, Artificial Intelligence (AI) has significantly impacted many industries, including higher education. More recently, this impact is accelerating with the rise of the immense potential of Generative AI (Gen-AI), equivalently Large Language Models (LLMs). This study aims to explore the potential capabilities and certain limitations of the Gen-AI tools in mathematics higher education and their impact on teaching. Specifically, the goal is to investigate how to use Gen-AI tools, namely different ChatGPTs for learning efficiently and in a secure way for a common mathematics course at universities. For this purpose, both the default versions (ChatGPT 3.5 and ChatGPT 4) and customised ChatGPT 4-based models are considered for the Year 1 Mathematics Calculus course. For that purpose, carefully curated questions covering different topics are considered to investigate the performance of the above-mentioned tools. The experimental findings are discussed in detail by highlighting the pros and cons of such advanced technologies in the educational landscape. Additionally, specific suggestions are discussed for the safe use of such tools without distracting students' learning processes. Relying on these course-specific findings, the underlined potential advantages or challenges of LLMs are aimed at being useful for their appropriate use in higher education. © 2024 Peter Lang Group AG, Lausanne.
