AB  - AI has transformed language acquisition, translation, communication, and more. This investigates how artificial intelligence has transformed language connection, looking at both historical and modern viewpoints, applications, difficulties, and potential future possibilities. Natural language processing (NLP), machine learning, and deep learning are examples of AI technologies that have greatly enhanced communication and language processing. AI has advantages, but it also has drawbacks, including bias, privacy issues, and ethical issues. This study emphasizes how critical it is to resolve these concerns to guarantee the ethical and responsible use of AI to improve multilingual communication and protect linguistic variety. © The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Switzerland AG 2025.
