AB  - Data science has emerged as a transformative force in the field of education and is revolutionizing by harnessing advanced applications and techniques, including computer vision, to analyze diverse data types. This chapter highlights the transformative potential of data science in education. It explores applications such as personalized learning, predictive analytics for student success, and optimizing educational resources. Techniques like machine learning used for predictive analysis, sentiment analysis, and natural language processing enable insights from text, multimedia, and assessment data. Computer vision enhances educational experiences through image and video analysis, automatic grading of handwritten assignments, and so on. With a wealth of data including student records, online behavior, and classroom interactions, data science empowers educators and institutions to make data-driven decisions, improve teaching, predict dropout allocation, and learning outcomes, and additionally contributes to curriculum development, adaptive testing, and educational research. This review chapter delves into the applications and techniques, with a particular focus on computer vision, and types of data that define the landscape of data science in education. © 2025 selection and editorial matter, Thangavel Murugan and W. Jai Singh; individual chapters, the contributors.
