AB  - This chapter dives into the transformative impact of artificial intelligence on learner-centric pedagogy, highlighting its role in tailoring education to diverse learning styles such as visual, auditory, and kinaesthetic. Through comprehensive research of novel pedagogics and the amalgamation of the visual, auditory, kinaesthetic (VAK) learning model, the work offers AI-enhanced strategies for personalizing learning practices. Case studies showcase pioneering real-time applications including AI-powered teaching assistants and adaptive learning programmes. Furthermore, this chapter voices significant ethical concerns, such as data privacy and fairness in AI applications. In order to endorse unbiasedness in an inclusive education, existing policies for responsible artificial intelligence in education are discussed. By exhibiting both the potential enhancements and the challenges created by AI in educational contexts, this chapter contributes to an extensive understanding of AI’s ability to offer learner-centric pedagogical preferences. © 2025 selection and editorial matter, Thangavel Murugan, Karthikeyan Periasamy, and A.M. Abirami; individual chapters, the contributors.
