AB  - The study, titled "AI in Academia: Pros and Cons of Integrating Artificial Intelligence in Universities," provides a thorough examination of the intricate dynamics involved in the use of AI in higher education. This research systematically examines academic literature and utilizes secondary data analysis to investigate the many elements of integrating artificial intelligence (AI), with a specific emphasis on both the potential benefits and the obstacles it poses. The approach entails doing a methodical examination of existing literature, using a diverse array of scholarly sources to develop a comprehensive comprehension of the present dialogue around artificial intelligence in academia. Secondary data analysis is used to reveal trends, settings. This technique guarantees a thorough analysis of the subject, using recognized academic criteria and discussions. Research findings reveal that AI has the capacity to profoundly transform educational methods and enhance administrative efficiency. However, it also raises notable ethical and practical issues, including data privacy, algorithmic prejudice, and its influence on employment inside academia. The report reveals an increasing tendency of colleges to use AI, showcasing a wide range of applications that span from customized learning to operational management. The research clearly highlights the two-sided character of AI integration at universities, emphasizing the need for a balanced approach that maximizes the advantages of AI while minimizing its hazards. Continual study and conversation are necessary within the academic community to navigate the intricate process of adopting AI, ensuring that it is in line with the core objectives of education and ethical norms. © The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Switzerland AG 2025.
