AU  - Lorenzo-Martín, M.E.
AU  - Fernández-Fernández, C.R.
AB  - The text analyses how Artificial Intelligence (AI) can be integrated into education to design contextualized learning situations that increase student motivation and promote equity. Through tools like ChatGPT, content can be personalized, and the curriculum can be connected to students’ local realities. The proposed methodology includes context analysis, definition of competencies, the use of prompts, and continuous evaluation with feedback. Additionally, the value of Universal Design for Learning (UDL) is highlighted as an inclusive framework. However, the implementation of AI entails ethical challenges such as data privacy, algorithmic bias, and the need for teacher training. The text concludes that AI should not replace teachers but complement them, and it advocates for inclusive policies and a culture of critical thinking to foster more motivating, personalized, and equitable education. © 2026 by IGI Global Scientific Publishing. All rights reserved.
