AB  - With the rapid development of artificial intelligence (AI), privacy risks associated with its applications have attracted increasing academic attention. This study uses CiteSpace to conduct a visual analysis of relevant literature from the Web of Science (2015-2025), aiming to identify research hotspots and trends. The findings reveal steady growth in research output, but limited collaboration among countries and institutions. A global network is emerging, with the United States and China as core research centres, and England and Australia as key hubs. The focus is shifting from technical issues to ethical concerns, particularly around data governance, generative model risks, and societal responses to AI decisions. © The Institution of Engineering & Technology 2025.
