TI  - The Impact of Artificial Intelligence on the Development of Strategies and Policies in the Field of Education
AU  - Liovas, D.
AB  - Artificial Intelligence (AI) has begun to significantly influence the shaping of strategies and policies in the field of education, offering new opportunities and challenges. One of the main impacts of AI is its ability to enable personalized learning. Through adaptive learning systems, AI can analyze the needs and abilities of each student, providing tailored educational material and support. This not only improves educational outcomes but also helps reduce inequalities, as students with different skill levels can progress at their own pace. Moreover, AI assists in improving the management of educational institutions. By automating tasks such as grading, attendance tracking, and resource management, educators can focus more on teaching and creating quality educational experiences. At the same time, AI can be used to predict trends and analyze data, helping schools and policymakers make informed decisions about resource allocation and the development of new curricula. © 2026 by IGI Global Scientific Publishing. All rights reserved.
