TI  - Adult Learning Theory Development and Its Role in Mentorship Framework
AU  - Karacheva, N.
AB  - This chapter analyzes key theories of adult education and their significance for modern mentoring models, reviewing conceptual foundations of Knowles’ andragogy, Kolb’s experimental learning model, Mezirow’s theory of transformational learning, and Tough’s concept of self-directed learning. Special attention is paid to methodological differences between these approaches and traditional pedagogical theories. The purpose of this study is to systematize the evolution of theoretical concepts about adult education and identify their contribution to effective mentoring practice. The chapter analyzes key concepts of each theory, critically evaluating their applicability, and identifying potential synergies between theories. The methodology is based on theoretical and comparative analyses of transdisciplinary sources, historical approaches to theory formation, and thematic analyses of mentorship. Results have practical significance for educators, mentors, trainers, and HR professionals, providing grounded, proven, and applicable tools for supporting professional growth. © 2026 by IGI Global Scientific Publishing. All rights reserved.
