TI  - Metaphorical perceptions and experiences of nursing students on using artificial intelligence tools: An exploratory descriptive qualitative study
AU  - Bahadir-Yilmaz, E.
T2  - Teaching and Learning in Nursing
AB  - Background: Artificial intelligence technologies offer a personalized learning experience that addresses individual student needs and promotes a sense of competence and engagement. Identifying students' perceptions and experiences regarding the use of artificial intelligence tools will be informative and guiding. Aim: This study investigated the metaphorical perceptions and experiences of students using artificial intelligence tools. Methods: An exploratory descriptive qualitative approach was used. This study was conducted with 73 nursing students in Türkiye. The data were collected from the students using a semi-structured interview form between February 6, 2025 and March 6, 2025. Colaizzi's descriptive phenomenological method was used for data analysis, which was carried out in seven stages. Results: Four main themes regarding students' use of artificial intelligence were identified as personalized learning, enhanced student engagement, immersive learning experiences, and perceived emotional difficulties. Conclusion: Students reported that the process was enjoyable, increased their motivation, provided a meaningful learning experience, enhanced their creativity, and gave them a sense of achievement. To enhance students’ participation and motivation in courses and learning processes, AI-supported programs should be utilized. © 2025 Organization for Associate Degree Nursing
