TI  - The impact of emerging educational technologies, including artificial intelligence and augmented reality, on the improvement of practical skills learning
AU  - Abbasi, E.
T2  - Educational Technology Research and Development
AB  - Background: Briefly describe the educational challenge, the relevance of AI and AR, and why improving practical skills learning is important. Purpose/Objective: State the primary aim of the study (to investigate the impact of AI and AR on practical skills learning) and any secondary aims (motivation, engagement, retention). Methods: Include study design (mixed-methods, quasi-experimental), participants, sampling, instruments (questionnaires, observations, interviews), intervention (AI + AR), and analysis methods. Results: Summarize the key findings: significantly higher post-test scores in the AI/AR group, improved motivation, engagement, satisfaction, and stronger 3-month retention relative to controls. Conclusion: Provide a concise interpretation that AI and AR effectively enhance practical skill acquisition and have important implications for education and training. © Association for Educational Communications and Technology 2025.
