TI  - Research on Student Achievement Prediction Based on XGBoostNet Attention Fusion Model
AU  - Han, Z.
AU  - Chen, L.
AB  - With the acceleration of educational informatization, online learning platforms have accumulated rich data on student behavior, providing new research opportunities for predicting student grades. However, existing prediction models still have significant limitations in fine-grained interaction modeling, complex feature processing, and interpretability. This study proposes an XGBoostNet Attention fusion model based on self attention mechanism to address the problems of insufficient recognition of extreme performance categories, inefficient feature interaction modeling, and poor training dynamics in traditional methods. This model achieves structural innovation through a dual optimization mechanism: firstly, a hybrid architecture of gradient boosting tree and self attention network is constructed, in which the XGBoost module dynamically evaluates the importance of features to generate initial weight distribution, and the self attention layer achieves dynamic weight reinforcement of key features through global interactive modeling; Secondly, a joint optimization strategy of feature gradient and attention weight is designed to accelerate the convergence process by suppressing redundant feature interference. The experimental results show that the model exhibits higher prediction accuracy and stability on multiple publicly available datasets. © 2025 IEEE.
