TI  - Enhancing Telecommunication Services With Artificial Intelligence and Statistical Analysis: Implications for Education and Future Employment
AU  - Abiad, M.
AB  - This chapter explores how artificial intelligence (AI) and statistical analysis can develop telecommunication services and their broader impact on education and the job market. We aim to demonstrate how AI technologies, like machine learning and predictive analytics, can improve service reliability, maintenance efficiency and customer relationship management (CRM). We delve into predictive maintenance and CRM strategies, discussing their theoretical and practical aspects. This includes examining the potential benefits, challenges in implementation and methods for predicting and managing customer churn using AI and statistical analysis. Furthermore, we investigate how advancements in AI and statistics should influence educational curricula, stressing the importance of integrating these technologies to better prepare students for future careers. The chapter also discusses new job categories and the skills needed in the AI-driven telecom sector to fulfil the changing needs of the job market. Our methodology includes a comprehensive review of existing research, conceptual analysis and practical examples of AI and statistical methods. This approach aims to give readers a deep understanding of AI’s role in improving telecommunication services and to provide valuable insights and best practices for implementation. The chapter enhances the knowledge of AI in telecommunications, offers practical insights for industry professionals, develops an educational framework for AI integration and recommends strategies for workforce development. This chapter contributes to the recent research about AI integration across various sectors, providing valuable guidance for educational institutions, policymakers and industry professionals. © 2025 Miltiadis Demetrios Lytras and Andreea Claudia Șerban.
