TI  - Artificial Intelligence and Performance Measurement Systems in Higher Education: Enhancing Faculty Evaluations and Organizational Outcomes
AU  - Alakoum, A.
AU  - Nica, E.
AB  - Introducing Artificial Intelligence (AI) in higher education institutions (HEIs) will transform faculty performance measurement systems (FPMS). Given the diverse contributions of academic staff, traditional evaluation methods often fail to measure this diversity in a way that is both efficient and sustaining. This chapter discusses how AI can improve these systems by increasing accuracy, effectiveness and individual feedback, leading to improved organizational outcomes. This chapter highlights available strengths and weaknesses, with case studies of AI-based solutions. For this, it would also use simulations and scenario analysis to predict more stringently where AI integration can bear fruit, what challenges are in sight and possible solutions. This chapter falls within the larger context of AI development and its impact on work, education and social organization tendencies opening new horizons for AI as transformers. This chapter guides policy recommendations and strategic insights for stakeholders to make the transition into an AI-powered future more palatable by combining technological developments with practical applications. © 2025 Miltiadis Demetrios Lytras and Andreea Claudia Șerban and 2025 The Authors.
