AU  - Saravanan, N.S.
AU  - Shankar, H.
AU  - Nivetha, S.
AB  - Conversational Learning is an intelligent educational assistant application that leverages multimodal AI to personalize the development of communication skills with dynamic real-time interaction experiences. This paper showcases an enhanced version of the system that brings together large language models (LLMs), speech-to-text processing, and contextually aware feedback to deliver immersive, adaptive learning experiences. The system integrates Google Gemini API, Google Text-to-Speech (gTTS) and speech recognition tools to create realistic communication experiences that fit the learner's profile. The system architecture involves a modular approach to present seamless deployment of the system as a web interface using Streamlit and React; while the backend services provide speech analytics and a prompt-driven dialogue. The platform also demonstrated the use of real-time grammar feedback, emotional tone assessment, and quiz customization generated by the AI. Through system validation and usability prior research studies, Conversational Learning has the potential to bridge the gap from knowledge to actionable communication. Most importantly, the system architecture is scalable and privacy-conscious and allows for integration with existing learning systems - an important feature for individual learning at an exciting time for place-based education involving AI. © 2025 IEEE.
