AB  - Innovation in technology is revolutionizing the education sector by creating new paradigms for teaching and learning. This chapter discusses the changes in educational environments due to emerging digital technologies such as artificial intelligence (AI), which makes learning opportunities more accessible while simultaneously making education more personalized, catering to individual needs. The chapter further delves into the various ways in which teaching approaches are enhanced by the advancements in technology, explaining how the automation of non-teaching functions enables educators to shift their attention toward nurturing creative thinking and emotional intelligence in learners. Furthermore, the chapter highlights the required considerations to address various challenges faced when integrating AI into education, making the need for the development and operationalization of ethical policies and frameworks lucid and clear. The study explores how technological integration, when collaborated with education, expands opportunities, especially for underserved communities, making it more accessible and opening new avenues for human-AI collaboration. © 2026 selection and editorial matter, K.M. Soni, Nitasha Hasteer, Aditi Bhardwaj, Rahul Sindhwani, and J., Paulo Davim; individual chapters, the contributors.
