AB  - With the rise of artificial intelligence (AI) and the unknown possibilities surrounding its evolution, contrasting reactions from teachers promoted different implementations of opportunities and constraints concerning the technology. However, research applying the Technological Pedagogical Content Knowledge (TPACK) framework highlights the dynamic nature of teacher knowledge transformation in an era of technology integration across classrooms, grade levels, and contexts. This chapter explores teachers’ development of TPACK as they experiment with emergent technologies like AI and integrate them creatively to promote deep learning in their classrooms. Examples from k-12 and higher education from a university-sponsored AI project illustrate some of the realities AI-powered tools have on pedagogical practices and developing TPACK. Alternately, constraints of AI-powered tools and policies are considered in the conversation. © 2026 selection and editorial matter, Michael Phillips, Evrim Baran, Punya Mishra, and Matthew J. Koehler; individual chapters, the contributors.
