AB  - Smart education technologies have a positive influence on students’ educational experience in general. This research aims to explore the utilization of smart education technologies in enhancing productivity and preparation for the job market specifically focusing on post-graduate students. The objectives include identifying the role of smart education technologies in enhancing the productivity of post-graduate students, increasing their career readiness, exploring their effectiveness compared to traditional education, and discovering smart education technologies utilized globally for benchmarking use. Primary and secondary data were gathered by assessing global cases of entities incorporating smart education technologies, distributing surveys to post-graduate students, and interviewing professors and educators to ensure alignment of both students’ and educators’ perspectives. The results revealed that utilizing smart education technologies can significantly enhance the overall educational experience of post-graduate students in terms of productivity and job readiness. © The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Switzerland AG 2025.
