AB  - Artificial intelligence is an extremely effective tool for teaching. By adapting the learning process to every student's unique learning style, degree of knowledge, comprehension, etc., AI customizes the learning process and makes it enjoyable and engaging for learners. AI also saves teachers money by streamlining a number of duties, including assessment and grading. By 2027, the education AI industry is projected to reach a size of over 25.7 billion USD in sales, growing at a compound annual growth rate (CAGR) of more than 40%. Approximately nine years from now! Many possibilities for careers in educational institutions will be created by AI. Particularly for individuals who have been already knowledgeable about and skilled in AI-based teaching. But since AI possesses emotional intelligence, it is unable to inspire students, something that's essential for learning. Thus, human intervention will always be necessary for AI to function properly. Thus, if AI and educators collaborate, they will be able to compensate for one another's shortcomings and function as a cohesive unit, enabling both students and educators to reach their full potential. AI is, in fact, a blessing in disguised for the field of education. © The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Singapore Pte Ltd. 2025.
