AB  - Background and purpose: This study addresses a critical gap in t echnological e ducation (TE) research by examining the integration of ChatGPT through the lens of s ocial l earning t heory (SLT). It investigates how ChatGPT adoption influences learners’ outcomes, lecturers’ instructional practices, and course development across individua l, organizational, and social dimensions. Methods: A mixed methods design was employed, combining the s ocial l earning t heory (SLT) with quantitative f actor a nalysis (FA) and qualitative t riangular e ntropy m atrix (TEM). This approach enabled the identificat ion of determinants of teaching effectiveness, learning performance, and course advancement within ChatGPT enabled t echnological e ducation (TE) contexts, while also clarifying both the benefits and challenges of its integration. Results and conclusions: Six key findin gs emerged. (1) P ersonalized l earning (PL CP) in teaching effectiveness is dr iven by p rofessional k nowledge a cquisition (PLA) and r eal time u pdated c ontent (RUC TE). (2) PL CP is further shaped by c ontinuous l earning (CL) and Interactive and Immersive Resources (IIR TE). (3) PLA is strongly linked to PL CP and R UC TE. (4) CL is influenced by c ontinuous l earning and u pdates (CLU CP) and IIR TE. (5) RUC TE is affected by PLA and PL CP. (6) IIR TE is shaped by CL and CLU CP. Collectively, these r esults highlight ChatGPT as a transformative tool in TE when situated within s ocial l earning t heory (SLT), advancing both pedagogical theory and practice. This research recommends structured implementation frameworks, faculty training initiatives, and curr iculum redesigns to optimize artificial intelligence AI integration. Future directions include longitudinal studies, cross cultural analyses, and comparative evaluations of AI enabled platforms in t echnological e ducation (TE). © 2025 The Author(s). Published by Informa UK Limited, trading as Taylor & Francis Group.
