TI  - The Role of AI in Enhancing Student Engagement and Motivation Through Personalized Learning
AU  - Sbaih, A.
AU  - Zeer, M.
AB  - As education shifts toward meeting each student's unique needs, artificial intelligence (AI) is stepping in as a game-changer to keep students engaged and excited about learning through personalized approaches. This paper dives into how AI can shake up education by crafting learning experiences that fit each student's strengths, struggles, and interests. With smart algorithms and tutoring systems, AI gives students feedback on the spot, tweaks lessons as they go, and even guesses what they'll need to learn next - making the whole process feel more lively and responsive. Plus, it throws in game-like features and adjusts to different learning styles, which can make lessons a lot more fun, especially for students who don't fit the usual mold or pace. That said, bringing AI into classrooms isn't all smooth sailing. There are real worries about keeping student info private, ensuring the tech plays fair for everyone, and making sure all kids - no matter where they come from - can actually use it. By digging into the latest research and real-life examples, this paper sheds light on both the cool possibilities and the tricky challenges of AI in personalized learning. It also tosses out some practical tips for teachers and tech folks on how to use AI in a way that's thoughtful and responsible, while pointing to a few ideas for future studies to crank up student motivation even more. In the end, it's all about showing how AI could not only help kids do better in school but also spark a love for learning that sticks with them for life. © 2025 IEEE.
