TI  - Understanding AI Integration Challenges in Education: A Brief Systematic Literature Review
AU  - Gouveia, A.J.
AU  - Costa, R.
AU  - Gomes, S.
AU  - Abreu, R.
AU  - Briga, L.
T2  - Communications in Computer and Information Science
AB  - This study explores the challenges of integrating Artificial Intelligence (AI) in education. As AI technology evolves, it has enormous potential to transform traditional teaching methods and improve learning outcomes. However, it also raises several difficulties, including ethical concerns, the lack of human interaction in classrooms due to automation processes, the need for teacher training, and inaccuracies in algorithms. This document aims to provide an in-depth analysis of the challenges and contributions associated with the incorporation of AI in education, using a systematic literature review. By addressing the key question and through data collection and analysis, this study offers insights into the challenges, benefits, and potential limitations of AI in education. The conclusions and discussions provide a comprehensive understanding of the current state of AI in education and its implications for students, teachers, and educational institutions. © The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Switzerland AG 2025.
