TI  - Enhancing Computer Programming Education: Integrating Advanced AI Tools for Challenging Curriculum Projects
AU  - Gouveia, A.J.
AU  - Machado, B.
AU  - Pendão, C.
T2  - Communications in Computer and Information Science
AB  - Integrating artificial intelligence (AI) tools into computer programming curricula offers significant benefits and challenges. Traditional computer programming education, reliant on theoretical classes, application exercises, and practical work to solve simple problems, has evolved with AI’s ability to solve conventional problems easily, complicating learning and assessment. While AI tools enhance problem-solving skills, critical thinking, and real-world applications, they also demand specialized AI knowledge, a robust understanding of programming fundamentals, and effective student evaluation. Addressing these challenges requires designing assignments that balance AI tool usage with creative application of programming knowledge. High-difficulty tasks that necessitate AI assistance but require students to construct the final solution themselves are proposed. This approach ensures students develop essential skills while leveraging AI, enriching their learning experience, and preparing them for the technological landscape. Integrating AI in programming education can thus significantly enhance students’ readiness for future careers. © The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Switzerland AG 2025.
