TI  - AI Applications in Education: Enhancing Human Creativity Through Collaborative Design
AU  - Agboola, O.P.
AU  - Yassin, Y.N.H.M.
T2  - Communications in Computer and Information Science
AB  - The swift incorporation of artificial intelligence (AI) into creative fields has brought about significant opportunities and challenges, especially in design and the creativity of human learning. This study explores the changing dynamics between AI-generated design and human creative processes, highlighting the interaction between technological advancements and human artistic insight. As AI systems grow more adept at producing innovative and visually appealing designs, the potential for collaboration between designers and AI becomes a vital area for investigation. This study looks into how AI can enhance human abilities, emphasizing methods to utilize AI to expand creative horizons without undermining the distinct contributions of designers. The ability of AI to assist in idea generation, optimize workflows, and inspire fresh design concepts is weighed against the necessity of keeping human oversight and decision-making central to the creative process. This pilot study-based research includes both qualitative and quantitative analyses of existing case studies that feature AI-human design partnerships, interviews with professionals who utilize AI tools, and 186 survey respondents assessing perceptions of AI’s role within the creative sector. The study also investigates frameworks for incorporating AI into educational environments, where it can help foster creativity and critical thinking skills among learners. The findings shed light on the elements that facilitate effective collaboration between AI and human designers, such as the significance of user-friendly interfaces, adaptable algorithms, and ethical considerations. Additionally, the study pinpointed best practices for creating a synergy that enhances both technological progress and human creativity. This research adds to the broader discussion about the future of creativity in a world influenced by AI by promoting a collaborative relationship between human and machine intelligence. © The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Switzerland AG 2025.
