TY  - CHAP
TI  - Introduction to Artificial Intelligence in Education
AU  - Sanmugam, M.
AU  - Zaini, K.M.
AU  - Lim, D.L.
T2  - Advances in Science, Technology and Innovation
AB  - Artificial intelligence (AI) has emerged as a transformative technology with the potential to revolutionise various sectors, including education. The integration of AI in education has gained significant attention in recent years. It has the potential to revolutionise teaching and learning practices, offering new opportunities for personalised instruction, adaptive assessment, and intelligent support systems. AI involves the development of computer systems capable of performing tasks that typically require human intelligence, such as language understanding, pattern recognition, decision-making, and data analysis. In the context of education, AI holds great potential to enhance teaching and learning experiences. Hence, this article explores the integration and impact of AI in education across all stages, from early childhood to higher education. AI facilitates personalised learning experiences in early childhood by adapting instructional approaches and content to meet young learners’ unique needs and learning styles. Intelligent tutoring systems provide individualised feedback, support, and guidance, promoting self-directed learning and academic success. AI in primary and secondary education holds great promise for empowering learners and transforming the learning experience. Adaptive learning platforms, intelligent tutoring systems, and immersive technologies like VR and AR provide personalised and engaging learning experiences. At the higher education stage, AI enhances teaching and administrative tasks. Automated grading systems streamline assessment processes, saving educators time and ensuring objectivity. AI algorithms analyse student profiles and data to provide personalised course recommendations, assisting students in making informed decisions. In conclusion, integrating AI in education across all stages can revolutionise teaching and learning by personalising learning experiences, facilitating adaptive instruction, and providing valuable insights. Balancing the benefits of AI with ethical considerations is essential for creating a comprehensive and effective educational ecosystem. However, responsible implementation, continuous evaluation, and ethical considerations are paramount to harness the full potential of AI in education and ensure equitable access and quality outcomes for all learners. © The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Switzerland AG 2025.
