TI  - Personalized AI-Driven Online Education Technologies for Adaptive Learning and Cognitive Skill Enhancement
AU  - Kumaresan, V.
AU  - Jeyakarthic, M.
AU  - Manjula Devi, P.
AU  - Jona Innisai Rani, P.
AU  - Mohan, E.
AU  - Surendra, K.R.
T2  - Proceedings of IEEE International Conference on Signal Processing,Computing and Control
AB  - The integration of artificial intelligence (AI) in online education is transforming learning experiences through personalized adaptive technologies. This study evaluates AI-driven online education platforms designed to enhance cognitive skills and learning adaptability. By leveraging machine learning algorithms and natural language processing, these platforms tailor content delivery based on learner profiles, real-time performance, and engagement patterns. A mixed-methods approach was adopted, involving data collection from user interaction logs, AI-driven personalization through reinforcement learning, and an experimental study with 500 students. Participants were divided into AI-personalized and conventional online learning groups, with evaluations conducted using knowledge retention tests, engagement analytics, and cognitive skill assessments. The findings reveal that AI-personalized learning improved knowledge retention by 28% and engagement levels by 35%, compared to conventional e-learning. Cognitive skill enhancement, including problem-solving and critical thinking, increased by 24%, while learning adaptability improved by 40% due to AI's dynamic content adjustments. Furthermore, 82% of students preferred AI-based adaptive learning over static online courses, highlighting its effectiveness in personalized education. These results emphasize the potential of AI-driven learning platforms in fostering individualized educational experiences and enhancing student outcomes. Future research will focus on refining AI models for greater adaptability and assessing their impact across diverse educational settings. © 2025 IEEE.
