TI  - Student Perceptions on AI Adoption and Integration in Higher Education
AU  - Shtayyat, A.
AU  - Gawanmeh, A.
AB  - This study investigates artificial intelligence (AI) adoption patterns and perceptual frameworks among university students through quantitative analysis. Statistical tests, including ANOVA and Chi-square, revealed no significant variations in AI familiarity across academic levels or correlations between faculty affiliation and usage frequency. Results demonstrate strong positive attitudes toward AI integration in education, with particular emphasis on personalized learning adaptation and information retrieval efficiency. Data privacy concerns emerged as critical mediating factors affecting adoption. The research proposes an evidence-based intervention framework encompassing psychological workshops, curriculum integration, and ethical guidelines. These findings contribute to the understanding of AI implementation in higher education, offering empirically-grounded recommendations for optimal technological integration within academic frameworks while addressing institutional and pedagogical considerations. © 2025 IEEE.
