TY  - CHAP
TI  - INTEGRATING WEAK GENERATIVE AI WITH PROJECT-BASED LEARNING: The LivePBL DEEP Method in Hybrid Music Education
AU  - Liu, Y.
AU  - Li, Y.
AU  - Zhao, T.
AB  - Generative Artificial Intelligence (GenAI) technologies indeed encounter several challenges in teaching and learning, particularly regarding efficiency, effectiveness, and scalability. These challenges stem from fragmented uses of the tools and a significant lack of a systematic method to navigate the design and implementation of applications. The LivePBL DEEP method addresses these issues by integrating project-based learning (PBL) with so called Weak GenAI (W-GenAI) through the DEEP method, that is, four design phases: Direction, Education, Event, and Project. Undertaking ChatGPT as an instance of W-GenAI, this chapter discusses and demonstrates the DEEP method’s research and development in a pilot hybrid music education project. Participants, including university students, school children, teachers, and community members, co-designed and implemented personalized learning sessions, workshops, and performances using ChatGPT. The findings indicate that, grounded in social constructivism, the DEEP method orientates the design of PBL loosely coupled with W-GenAI applications. These coupled interactions align with personalized learning goals across diverse educational settings, improving engagement through collaborative and social experiences, widening participatory and inclusive learning opportunities, and ultimately enhancing personalized learning. Therefore, this approach ensures the adaptability and scalability of W-GenAI in PBL. © 2025 selection and editorial matter, Mahmoud Elkhodr and Ergun Gide.
