TI  - GENAI IN SPECIAL EDUCATION: A Case of Teaching and Learning GenAI for Design in Hong Kong Special Schools
AU  - Liu, X.
AU  - Lau, N.
AU  - Maximo, T.
AB  - Generative Artificial Intelligence (GenAI) has been increasingly applied to special education in recent years. This study explores the potential of GenAI to enhance special education. The researchers first reviewed the concepts in special education and the main applications of GenAI in this field. A lack of GenAI education in special schools was identified. To explore this gap, the researchers conducted a case study in Hong Kong special schools, investigating students’ experiences of learning and using text-to-image GenAI design tools. The findings indicated generally positive experiences toward teaching and learning GenAI among the participating students, teachers, and social workers, though challenges and strengths emerged. Drawing on the findings, the researchers discussed the potential for and concerns about incorporating GenAI education into special schools. In addition, recommendations were provided for implementing GenAI education in special education practices. This study contributes to the exploration of leveraging emerging GenAI technologies to support students with special educational needs (SEN) in their learning and growth. © 2025 selection and editorial matter, Mahmoud Elkhodr and Ergun Gide.
