AB  - The integration of artificial intelligence (AI) into educational practices holds immense promise for transforming both learning experiences and teaching methodologies. AI technologies, including ma chine learning and natural language processing, enable personalized learning experiences tailored to individual student needs, thereby enhancing engagement and effectiveness. Moreover, AI-driven systems automate administrative tasks such as assessment and scheduling, allowing educators to allocate more time to instructional activities. However, alongside these benefits, significant ethical considerations arise, including issues related to data privacy, algorithmic bias, and equitable access to AI tools. Addressing these challenges is crucial to ensuring that AI in education is deployed responsibly and inclusively. © 2025 by IGI Global Scientific Publishing. All rights reserved.
