TI  - Travel Planning with Artificial Intelligence: Virtual Assistants and Recommendation Systems
AU  - Balawardhana, M.
AB  - This chapter examines the transformative impact of artificial intelligence (AI) on travel planning, with a special focus on conversational AI technologies like virtual assistants (VAs). By leveraging machine learning and natural language processing (NLP), VAs enhance personalised travel experiences, automating processes such as itinerary planning, booking, and real-time adjustments. Scandinavian countries, renowned for their innovative technology applications, serve as case studies, particularly Finland’s use of AI to optimise Northern Lights tourism. However, despite its benefits, AI in travel planning raises concerns about data privacy, algorithmic bias, and ethical challenges related to over-personalisation and data manipulation for commercial interests. Addressing these challenges requires collaborative efforts from stakeholders, including regulatory bodies, to implement transparent, inclusive, and ethical AI systems. The chapter also discusses emerging AI integrations with augmented and virtual reality (AR/VR) and the Internet of Things (IoT), exploring how these technologies can provide immersive and efficient travel experiences. With a focus on future trends, it highlights how AI can address sustainability concerns in tourism while noting the importance of data protection and unbiased algorithms to ensure fair access. As AI continues to advance, its role in shaping global travel planning grows increasingly pivotal. © 2025 selection and editorial matter, Maria Jesus Jerez-Jerez, Claudia Sevilla-Sevilla, and Lidia Aguiar-Castillo.
