TI  - Beyond Pandora’s Box: Safeguarding Education with a Bridge to an Effective AI
AU  - Akash, R.
AU  - Suganya, V.
AB  - While artificial intelligence (AI) offers exciting possibilities for personalized learning and enhanced educational experiences, concerns exist regarding potential biases, security risks, and the overall impact on human educators. This chapter delves into this complex landscape, drawing parallels to the metaphorical “Pandora’s Box” – a mythical artifact that unleashed both blessings and curses. Our main objective is to carefully construct a conceptual framework that connects the potential advantages and inherent hazards of AI in the field of education. This approach will act as a guide for protecting educational institutions while facilitating the efficient incorporation of AI technologies for a stronger learning environment. This chapter employs a rigorous conceptual approach. We build our foundation upon a comprehensive literature review, meticulously examining existing knowledge and insights on AI in education. Through this review, we will identify key themes, challenges, and opportunities associated with AI adoption in educational settings. Ultimately, our chapter seeks to propose a set of succinct research propositions that guide future empirical investigations into responsible AI implementation within the educational domain. These propositions will stem from the insights gleaned from the literature review and the conceptual model we construct. By outlining these propositions, we aim to stimulate further research and pave the way for the development of practical frameworks for safe and effective AI use in education. © 2025 Babita Singla, Kumar Shalender and Nripendra Singh.
