TI  - Exploring the Impact of AI Tools on Student Engagement, Learning Outcomes, and Wellbeing: A Multivariate Analysis
AU  - Bhimavarapu, U.
AB  - This study investigates the effectiveness of AI tools in enhancing student satisfaction within university education, using advanced data analysis techniques to capture nuanced student emotions and measure their satisfaction levels. Traditional methods, such as linear regression and decision trees, often fall short in evaluating complex, nonlinear interactions among the factors influencing student happiness with AI tools. To address these limitations, this study integrates Multivariate Adaptive Regression Splines (MARS) and Convolutional Neural Networks (CNNs) as part of an innovative methodological framework. MARS is employed for its capacity to model nonlinear relationships and identify the most impactful factors, providing insights into specific elements of AI tools that significantly affect student satisfaction. In parallel, CNNs are utilized to analyze unstructured data, such as text feedback and engagement patterns, enabling deeper pattern recognition in student emotions. © 2025 by IGI Global Scientific Publishing. All rights reserved.
