TI  - AI and Social Networks: A Transformative Partnership for Education
AU  - Lui, K.
AB  - The advent of social networks has undoubtedly changed the way we disseminate information, communicate, and interact with one another. The ways in which AI and social networking are beneficial for higher education have come under much scrutiny. This chapter examines multifaceted roles that AI and social networks play. The chapter starts with the historical context of the social learning theories, reflects the birth and rise of digital networking and differentiates between social networks as used in teaching practices. It also elaborates on possible advantages of the integration of social networks and AI in the context of education as well as the risks it could bring. It also provides a series of case studies in which social networks have been used in successful ways and across different educational contexts. This examination offers insights and strategies for educators, administrators, and policymakers to more successfully implement social networks within education creating richer, more engaging, collaborative, digitally fluent learning contexts. © 2025 by IGI Global Scientific Publishing. All rights reserved.
