TI  - Leveraging Technology for Ethical and Sustainable Global Development
AU  - Bhutani, V.
AU  - Singh Bahadur, P.S.
AU  - Sansaniwal, S.K.
AB  - In today’s rapidly evolving world, technology is at the forefront of significant global changes. Innovations such as artificial intelligence (AI), blockchain, renewable energy, and biotechnology are not only shaping industries but are also becoming critical tools in addressing pressing global challenges. These technologies hold immense potential to solve issues related to poverty, inequality, healthcare, and climate change. Yet, as these technologies advance, they bring complex ethical challenges and raise questions about the adequacy of existing policies to manage their development and deployment. This chapter will explore how emerging technologies can serve as a catalyst for global development while addressing the ethical concerns and policy challenges they bring. By examining real-world examples and interdisciplinary insights, the chapter will provide a balanced perspective on how innovation can be harnessed for progress while considering the ethical frameworks and policies needed to guide their responsible use. © 2025 by IGI Global Scientific Publishing. All rights reserved.
