TI  - Developing a Framework for Implementing AI in Education and Evaluating Its Use
AU  - de Leon, L.
AB  - The purpose of this chapter is to create a framework for implementing AI in education through a systematic synthesis process. This chapter utilized a synthesis method for frameworks proposed originally by Carroll et al. (2011) and further elaborated by Cardoso Ermel et al. (2021). They propose four procedural steps, which were followed in this chapter. The steps included several iterations of literature review to refine and support the framework that gradually developed. Through the synthesis method, the Nested Framework for Implementing AI in Education emerged, with three levels that were categorized as Institutional Transformation, Ethical Practice, and AI-Driven Personalized Learning. © 2025 selection and editorial matter, Joseph Rene Corbeil and Maria Elena Corbeil; individual chapters, the contributors.
