AB  - In the field of electrical engineering, artificial intelligence (AI) has become a game-changing instrument that is transforming management and education. This study examines the various ways AI can improve project management, educational strategies, and electrical engineering procedures. Through the use of predictive analytics, resource allocation optimisation, and real-time electrical system recording, AI-powered systems in management improve decision-making. These elements ensure the drawn-out execution of undertakings, enormously decline margin time, and increment functional viability. Through virtual labs, modern showing structures, and customized opportunities for growth, simulated intelligence driven advancements are reforming instructing and learning draws near. Calculations for versatile learning fulfill the needs of every individual student and give a more profound understanding of complex electrical designing thoughts. Moreover, by giving understudies genuine encounter without the limits of actual gear, virtual labs and recreation apparatuses assist with shutting the hole among hypothetical comprehension and certifiable application. To completely use computer-based intelligence, this concentrate likewise examines issues that should be settled, including information insurance, moral worries, and the abilities hole. Electrical designing can possibly arrive at up 'til now unfathomable degrees of imagination, effectiveness, and availability through the joining of man-made intelligence in administration and training. The outcomes feature how significant computer-based intelligence will be in moving electrical designing improvements later on, making the way for additional shrewd frameworks and profoundly qualified specialists. A worldview change is shown by the joint effort among artificial intelligence and electrical designing administration and schooling, which will make the field more powerful, versatile, and in accordance with the necessities of a world that is turning out to be all the more mechanically progressed. © 2025 IEEE.
