AB  - This conceptual article explores how artificial intelligence (AI) could transform education in the next 50 years. It envisions a society with high share of workless individuals where AI is utilized for the common good. The study curricula will focus on developing human skills, promoting co-existence, collaboration, and co-construction of knowledge with AI, ensuring the acquisition of necessary skills for species survival in the case of a technology breakdown. The article highlights the shift toward personalized and flexible learning environments, the implications for teachers, assessment, grading, and certifications. It discusses the ethical considerations of this scenario, emphasizing the responsible AI use. © 2025 Taylor & Francis Group, LLC.
