AU  - Shah, M.
AB  - This study gives an overview of the possible advantages and difficulties of applying machine learning (ML) algorithms in education. The chapter emphasizes the value of careful planning and taking ethical issues into account when utilizing ML in education and asserts that more research is required to fully investigate ML’s potential to improve teaching and learning. Here, we examine how ML is being used in education. Predictive analytics, personalized learning, intelligent tutoring systems, natural language processing recommender systems, and learning analytics are a few of the domains where ML can be used. One of the major insights of this study is that ML has the ability to greatly enhance student results by delivering individualized and efficient instruction. Students who are in danger of academic failure can be identified using predictive analytics, and personalized learning can offer learning paths specifically designed to meet the needs of each student. The study also discusses some of the difficulties in applying ML algorithms in education, including issues with privacy, prejudice, and ethical considerations. To guarantee that the potential advantages of ML are achieved while limiting any negative effects, the necessity of thorough planning and execution methodologies is highlighted. © 2025 selection and editorial matter, Shruti Sharma, Ashutosh Sharma, and Trinh Van Chien.
