AB  - In recent years, under the context of rapid development of information technology, the demand for personalized teaching in higher vocational computer courses has become increasingly high, and the shortcomings of traditional teaching methods have become prominent, making it impossible to meet the diverse learning needs brought by modern information technology development. This study mainly uses machine learning and advanced technologies to create a personalized tutoring and optimization system to enhance students' learning outcomes. The research primarily applies the Random Forest and Collaborative Filtering algorithms, using these two algorithms to analyze students' learning data and formulate personalized learning paths for users. In this paper, the method is analyzed based on 5000 pieces of student data. By using the Random Forest to classify students' knowledge mastery and combining it with the Collaborative Filtering algorithm to recommend personalized resources, the system operation logic is formed. The experiment shows that, compared to the control group's improvement rate of 8.26%, the average improvement rate of students in the experimental group reached 11.29%, with the best result improving by 15.38%. This fully demonstrates the effectiveness of the system in improving learning efficiency and provides a new technical solution for personalized teaching in higher vocational education. © 2025 SPIE.
