AB  - This chapter examines professors' perspectives on using risk-free artificial intelligence (AI) in higher education classrooms, focusing on the perceived benefits, challenges, and ethical considerations surrounding AI implementation. Researchers gathered insights into professors' experiences and viewpoints on integrating AI into educational settings through a qualitative study using a survey method, semi-structured interviews, and questionnaires. The findings reveal that while AI offers substantial opportunities for enhancing teaching and learning, it also brings notable challenges and ethical concerns. Based on these insights, the chapter recommends best practices to ensure the responsible and effective use of AI tools in higher education. © 2025, IGI Global Scientific Publishing.
