AB  - This chapter examines the effect of Artificial Intelligence (AI) on the education sector, focusing on its use and effects in executive structures, educational processes, and outcomes. The methodology involved an assessment of AI applications recognized through elementary examination. AI, along with human- like reasoning abilities, has significantly influenced training approaches in educational institutions. The study also investigates into the intersection of climate resilience and education, emphasizing AI's transformative potential in allowing communities to address rising climate change challenges. By leveraging AI- based educational strategies, communities can enhance their considerate of climate change impacts, adjust to changing conditions, and mitigate associated risks. The chapter aims how AI- enabled education can serve as a catalyst for community empowerment in building climate resilience. Through a detailed inspection of AI applications, the study aims to equip communities with the knowledge, skills, and tools necessary to thrive amidst a changing climate landscape. © 2025, IGI Global. All rights reserved.
