AB  - In this study, we propose an innovative model based on artificial intelligence for predicting and managing student behaviors by addressing the complexity and sparsity of student behaviors in campus big data. First, the problem of insufficient behavioral characterization and timeliness of labels is solved by establishing a cross-modal student behavioral portrait model based on deep learning of multimodal features. Secondly, an effective early warning method for abnormal student behavior is proposed by combining long and short-term memory neural networks and multi-indicator data. Experiments confirm that the method is better than traditional algorithms in terms of accuracy and timeliness, and can effectively improve the effect of student behavior prediction and management, and promote the application of personalized education and behavior prediction. © 2024 The Authors.
