TI  - Artificial Intelligence Application in K-12 Education
AU  - Singh, A.P.
AU  - Mathur, S.
AU  - Fancy, C.
T2  - AIP Conference Proceedings
AB  - Artificial Intelligence is a cutting-edge innovation that might revolutionize K-12 education system. In this literature review, we explore the relationship between AI and K-12 education research. We categorize the findings based on the analysis of several investigative components. We examine the many applications of AI in education and organize them into 24 subcategories in addition to four primary categories: performance, behavior, teaching, and student selection. AI and education have had a tremendous influence on the educational system. It is feasible to teach these systems to become more intelligent, which will enable them to handle challenging issues like purpose, feelings, standards of morality, and behaviour. As a result of individual devices' progress and computer systems, AI has grown so far that it can now be seen in a variety of industries. Moreover, the capacity to connect machine-based technology to other device or machines is significantly responsible for the widespread application of AI. In conclusion, this project highlights the potential of AI for K-12 in the education system. Policymakers and stakeholders should devise a strategy to make learning simpler and more effective by integrating AI technologies into numerous education-related sectors. As a result, teachers may be more effective in the classroom, and students can benefit from higher-quality learning opportunities. This information is crucial for researchers to improve the significance and value of their work forfuture studies. © 2024 American Institute of Physics Inc.. All rights reserved.
