TY  - CHAP
TI  - Evaluation of Artificial Intelligence tools (ChatGPT and Google Bard) in higher education for the history of America: Answering questions and crafting assignments with a gender perspective
AU  - Carrasco-Rodríguez, A.
AB  - This study explores the use of Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools, specifically ChatGPT-4 and Google Bard, on the teaching of American history in the context of higher education. It aims to evaluate the accuracy and relevance of these tools generating historical content, as well as their ability to integrate gender perspective and the use of inclusive language. The study procedure included preparing multiple-choice questions, short-answer questions, essay questions, and practical assignments to assess the capabilities of both AI tools. Mixed, quantitative, and qualitative evaluation criteria were applied to analyze historical accuracy, argumentation, inclusion of gender perspective and writing and style. The results revealed a marked difference between the two tools. ChatGPT-4 demonstrated a high degree of accuracy and ability to create solid arguments, significantly outperforming Google Bard, which showed significant deficiencies in several of the evaluated aspects. The study highlights academic concerns about the misuse of AI by students and the ethical implications of its use. At the same time, it recognizes the possibilities AI offers to support teaching, if used as a complementary tool and not as a substitute for traditional learning. Recommendations are proposed to improve AI integration in education and future research lines are suggested to further explore the impact of AI in different disciplines and educational levels. © 2024 Peter Lang Group AG, Lausanne. Published by Peter Lang GmbH, Berlin, Germany. All rights reserved.
