AB  - The development of brain science has promoted our understanding of intelligence theory, which has had a profound impact on modern education. In this study, we started from the transformation course of education mode since the establishment of the People's Republic of China, exploring the intrinsic connection between the development of science and technology and the change in education, and focused on the impact of brain science and technology and theories on higher music education in China in the context of brain science and technology and theories. The technology of virtual simulation enables the intuitive presentation of brain science research findings to scholars and students in the field of education. We took the "Psychology of Music Education"course as an example. Based on brain science and neuroscience research results, students can understand the role of the brain and nerves in music activities. Additionally, through the utilization of virtual simulation, they gain a nuanced understanding of the psychological characteristics of music learning, exploring both its universal and specific aspects. It has been proven that this approach can help students to master the scientific development of the modern psychology of music education, and improve the teaching effect of the psychology of music education. This will help students to master the scientific development of modern music education psychology and ultimately improve the teaching outcomes within music education. © 2024 IEEE.
