TI  - Effect of artificial intelligence on education
AU  - Karmakar, S.
AU  - Das, T.
AB  - Education and artificial intelligence (AI) are two fields that have recently intersected, and their convergence has created exciting new possibilities for the future of education. AI technology can enhance the learning experience by providing personalized content, immediate feedback, and advanced analytics to help teachers and students make informed decisions. AI-powered educational tools such as adaptive learning systems, intelligent tutoring systems, and learning analytics can improve students’ engagement, motivation, and learning outcomes. These tools can identify students’ strengths and weaknesses, personalize learning paths, and provide real-time feedback to improve their learning experience. The integration of AI into education also raises concerns about the ethical and social implications of using technology to automate teaching and learning. AI must be designed with transparency, accountability, and inclusiveness to ensure that it benefits all students regardless of their background, abilities, or disabilities. This chapter examines AI applications, encompassing machine learning and deep learning, and their implications for student engagement, personalization, and learning outcomes. While acknowledging the immense potential of AI, this chapter also delves into its challenges. The ethical considerations surrounding data privacy and the potential for overreliance on technology are scrutinized. © 2025 selection and editorial matter, Irfan Ali, Umar Muhammad Modibbo, Asaju La’aro Bolaji and Harish Garg.
