AU  - Tyagi, A.
AB  - Career planning for college students is significantly influenced by career choices, which can be a daunting decision in today's society. Many students are uncertain about their future paths despite having various talents and skills. Our innovative approach to student career advising integrates machine learning (ML) for job prediction with a user-friendly chatbot interface, aiming to provide a comprehensive solution to this issue. The ML-based career prediction model analyzes several factors, including students' talents, educational backgrounds, and interests. We compared three ML algorithms - KNN, Random Forest, and Decision Tree - finding KNN to be the most accurate with a 97% success rate. The application, developed using Flutter and Google API, features a chatbot that answers career-related queries, allows appointment bookings, and includes a FAQ page. The website, designed with Flask, HTML, Jinja2, and Scikit-learn, offers a login system and a career prediction tool that assesses users' proficiency in various fields through a series of questions. It then suggests appropriate job fields, necessary skills, job locations, salary information, and relevant courses, enhancing the overall career counseling experience. This dual strategy ensures students receive dynamic and personalized guidance, helping them make informed decisions about their professional futures. © 2024 IEEE.
