TI  - Using AI-Powered Tools in Language Education: Should They Be Allowed or Banned?
AU  - Çelik, S.
AU  - Karaca, B.
AB  - This study explores the beliefs and perspectives of pre-service language teachers (PSLT) regarding the use of artificial intelligence (AI) tools in language education. The study seeks to determine the AI tools being utilized, their effects on learning experiences, and PSLT’s plans for integrating these technologies into their teaching practices. With this aim in mind, semi-structured interviews were conducted with ten PSLTs who have prior experience with AI-powered language learning tools. The results show that AI-powered tools can have a positive effect on language education experiences, and they also highlight the need for ethical considerations and responsible application to ensure integration is fair and efficient. The findings also provide recommendations for educators to maximize the benefits of using AI tools in language classrooms. © 2024 by Nova Science Publishers, Inc.
