AU  - Tan, L.P.
AB  - This chapter aims to establish a network and map of research on ChatGPT in education based on 136 publications from the Web of Science database. Two bibliographic analysis methods, bibliographic coupling and co-citation, were used to discover publication rank and key clusters according to each method. This allowed for the identification of influential publications, authors, and journals. The results of this chapter will assist researchers in positioning their research, identifying potential topics for future studies, and enabling knowledge about the use of ChatGPT in education to make it more accessible to students, new researchers, and policymakers. This chapter pioneers the exploration of networks and maps in the study of ChatGPT in education by utilizing two methods of bibliographic analysis. © 2025 selection and editorial matter, Mohamed Lahby.
