AB  - This study investigates the possibilities of artificial intelligence (AI) in Indian higher education institutions (HEI). The inquiry focuses on the impact of responsible AI on the adoption of AI and the role of employee engagement in influencing this relationship. The study employed quantitative research methods, doing confirmatory factor analysis (CFA) using AMOS and utilizing SPSS for mediation analysis. The report asserts that the implementation of responsible AI practices and the active involvement of leadership are essential for the successful adoption of AI. The future of education relies heavily on the ethical use of AI and the presence of proactive leadership. © 2024 IEEE.
