AB  - AI is having a game-changing impact on how we learn and teach. Private AI, employed by a single educational institution, can offer personalized learning experiences for students, automate teacher duties, and develop innovative educational tools. Employing AI-powered systems, personalized learning assesses individual needs and dynamically adapts training, thereby maximizing learning efficacy and effectiveness through engaging and enjoyable content. AI-powered tuition systems can also provide on-demand assistance for students struggling in specific fields or those seeking efficient tools for exam preparation. While proponents of private AI in education envision a future characterized by personalized assessments and enhanced student potential, the financial hurdles associated with establishing and utilizing such technology cannot be dismissed. The prohibitive cost of development and implementation poses a significant challenge, potentially jeopardizing the accessibility of this innovative approach for smaller institutions. Another issue is ensuring the ethical and responsible application of AI systems, such as avoiding prejudice against students or privacy invasion. As private AI in education continues to expand, educational institutions must carefully assess their requirements and goals before investing in these systems and take steps to ensure their moral and accountable usage. © 2025 selection and editorial matter, Uma Maheswari V and Rajanikanth Aluvalu; individual chapters, the contributors.
