TY  - CHAP
TI  - Artificial Intelligence Driven Nanobiosensors Virus Detection and Precision Medicine
AU  - Dave, A.
AB  - Modern healthcare practices, such as personalized medicine, use data on each patient’s own clinical constitution to realize early illness intervention based on better-informed medical choices. In this context, the use of diagnostic instruments in conjunction with measurement evaluation that can be carried out in a trustworthy and automated manner is crucial. With the help of cutting-edge point-of-care (PoC) devices and machine learning algorithms, risk assessments for a variety of ailments may now be carried out accurately and affordably. In this chapter, the argument is made that PoC testing combined with risk assessments created using artificial intelligence (AI) algorithms, used to screen the entire population for several conditions at once, represents a new type of inexpensive screening that can result in the early detection of diseases and other positive effects on public health. Because of its low-cost components, small size, and user-friendly operation, point-of-care testing (POCT) is gaining more and more attention. POCT is frequently less accurate than conventional laboratory tests and assays, though. Algorithms based on AI have the potential to dramatically enhance the performance of PoC sensors by quantifying the signals.
