AB  - This chapter examines perceptions and usage of generative artificial intelligence among university students in the field of management. It starts with a literature review regarding key aspects of this topic. Then, it explores how students interact with generative artificial intelligence and investigates their expectation towards it as well as the outcomes it creates. In a qualitative study, the chapter investigates patterns and themes providing comprehensive insights into the aspects influencing user perception and usage of generative artificial intelligence by means of semi-structured interviews. The explorative methodology uncovers four themes that emerged in the data analysis: lack of tangibility, benefits, drawbacks, and skill development. Based on these findings, the chapter proposes five research questions that should be addressed by future research. © (Publication Year), (publisher Name). All rights reserved.
