AB  - This chapter offers a comprehensive exploration of integrating artificial intelligence (AI) into early childhood education, bridging theoretical foundations with practical applications. It begins by providing key educational theories, to establish a developmental framework for AI integration. The chapter then reviews current AI applications in early learning environments, analyzing their benefits and limitations through recent research and case studies. Practical examples demonstrate AI's role in personalized learning, language development, and social-emotional learning. Ethical considerations are also thoroughly discussed. The chapter concludes by discussing and providing actionable recommendations for educators, policymakers, and researchers to ensure ethical and effective AI integration in early childhood education. This chapter serves as an authoritative resource for stakeholders aiming to enhance early childhood education through AI. © 2025 by IGI Global Scientific Publishing. All rights reserved.
