AU  - Zolfaghari, M.
AU  - Salamzadeh, A.
AU  - Afsharpour, O.
AB  - In the rapidly evolving fields of education, entrepreneurship, and artificial intelligence, understanding the applications of AI in educational entrepreneurship is essential. This chapter adopts an applied research approach, using qualitative methods such as a systematic literature review and semi-structured interviews with 14 experts from education, entrepreneurship, and AI. Through thematic analysis, 1830 initial themes were distilled into 42 first-level themes, categorized into 20 second-level themes, and ultimately consolidated into three overarching themes. These global themes reveal AI's impact on enhancing learning productivity, streamlining instructional methods, and advancing educational administration and leadership. The findings underscore AI's transformative potential in educational entrepreneurship, providing a comprehensive framework highlighting AI's diverse contributions to the education system. © 2025 by IGI Global Scientific Publishing. All rights reserved.
