TI  - Impact of Generative Artificial Intelligence on Journalism: Practice and Deontology
AU  - Harb, W.A.M.
AU  - Qabajeh, M.
AB  - The use of artificial intelligence (AI) in journalism has raised questions about the role of journalists, the accuracy of AI-generated content, and the industry’s ethical responsibilities. Generative AI technologies have transformed news production, enabled automated content generation, and enhanced efficiency. This chapter explores the challenges and opportunities journalists have faced with AI and examines its current applications such as natural language processing and automated content creation. It also discusses the benefits of AI, like increased efficiency and accuracy, while addressing associated risks and ethical considerations. The evolving role of journalists in an AI-driven world is analyzed, emphasizing the importance of ethical considerations and critical thinking in AI implementation. AI integration challenges traditional journalistic values of accuracy, accountability, and transparency. The authenticity and verifiability of AI-generated content have become critical concerns as the line between human-authored and AI-generated material blurs. Moreover, the potential for bias in AI algorithms necessitates vigilance to ensure unbiased reporting. Journalists have a responsibility to uphold professional standards and provide reliable information. They must critically evaluate and fact-check AI-generated content before dissemination. This chapter provides an overview of the evolving landscape of journalism in the AI era, highlighting both opportunities and challenges. It emphasizes ethical considerations and the need for journalists to navigate AI integration while preserving integrity and accountability in their reporting. © The Editor(s) (if applicable) and The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Switzerland AG 2024.
