TI  - Innovations of AI in Primary School’s Learning: A Systematic Review
AU  - Sin, A.C.K.
AU  - Barkhaya, N.M.M.
AB  - Inclusive education offers equitable learning opportunities for all students, regardless of their backgrounds or abilities. This paper explores the potential of artificial intelligence can be leveraged to overcome barriers in public school, focusing on primary level to ensuring inventive, invaluable and inclusive learning experiences. Through a systematic review, the study investigates how AI can foster accessible and inclusive learning in primary level. A structured systematic literature review approach was employed to analyze 20 studies from 2020 to 2024. Through detailed case studies and theoretical discussions, it examines various innovations of AI integral to inclusive education, such as AI- driven personalized learning, virtual classrooms, and technology- enhanced teacher training. These innovations contribute significantly to making education more accessible. By aligning with the goals of Sustainable Development Goal 4, this paper underscores the transformative potential of AI in fostering the accessibility of instructional tools and creating inclusive educational environments. © 2025 by IGI Global Scientific Publishing. All rights reserved.
