AU  - Torres, J.R.
AU  - López-Cirugeda, I.
AB  - This chapter explores undergraduate and adult learners’ attitudes toward integrating AI-enabled educational technologies into L1 and L2 teaching and learning environments. The research was conducted through a survey and data was collected to understand students’ key preferences and concerns about integrating AI into education. The results show a distinct range of attitudes among participants and highlight either positive reactions, such as the appreciation for personalised feedback; or negative concerns, such as fears about reduced human interaction and privacy. Also, relevant pedagogical implications, recommendations for educators, and suggestions for future research are discussed to support the integration of AI into syllabus education. © 2025 by IGI Global Scientific Publishing. All rights reserved.
