AB  - The complexity of modern software systems necessitates adaptability to better handle complex environments. This paper, from an object-oriented perspective, investigates adaptive learning methods using software agent technology. The study thoroughly examines the software engineering issues of adaptive systems from four perspectives: model, mechanism, language, and platform. The project integrates reinforcement learning and software agent technology, delving into the adaptive mechanisms of reinforcement learning, constructing adaptive intelligent agent software models, and exploring frameworks for adaptive system construction and adaptive learning algorithms. The case analysis of a robotic dog demonstrates that through continuous interaction with the environment, the robotic dog updates its understanding of the environment in real time, allowing it to adjust its strategy to adapt to changes in prey movement patterns and promptly adjust its role to replenish energy as needed to complete its tasks. This research validates the effectiveness of the proposed models, mechanisms, languages, and platforms, highlighting the potential impact of adaptive systems in enhancing system stability. © 2024 IEEE.
