AU  - Baroud, S.Y.
AU  - Qureshi, M.N.
AB  - The emergence of Industry 4.0 marks a transformative era characterized by advanced technologies. These innovations promise significant advantages, including enhanced productivity, sustainable progress and heightened resilience. However, integrating these technologies poses challenges, notably the need for a skilled workforce proficient in information technology and data analytics. This study proposes a comprehensive framework for integrating Artificial Intelligence (AI), Machine Learning (ML), Deep Learning (DL), Multi-Agent Systems (MAS) and Extended Reality (XR) technologies into educational games (EDs) to improve personalized learning, foster engagement and enhance outcomes as a proof of concept. We employed a mixed-methods approach, combining quantitative and qualitative data to provide a holistic view of the framework's effectiveness. The outcomes indicate that integrating advanced technologies in EDs significantly enhances learning outcomes, supports critical thinking and fosters motivation. However, challenges such as technical complexity, data privacy and ethical considerations. This study discusses these findings' practical implications and offers future research and development recommendations. By addressing the previous challenges, the proposed framework aims to prepare individuals for the digital age, fostering a skilled, resilient and responsible workforce. © 2024 IEEE.
