AU  - Ramadhani, D.S.
AU  - Rozalina, D.
T2  - AIP Conference Proceedings
AB  - Artificial intelligence in the counseling profession is one of the fields developing using computer technology and the internet. The challenge for counselors is to make computer and internet technology a profitable means of accessing dynamic, innovative, and prospective education and counseling services and how this can strategically impact the quality of education and counseling services. This paper attempts to provide an overview of research on artificial intelligence (AI) in the counseling profession through a systematic review. The results show that most of the disciplines involved in AIC come from computer science and the internet. The synthesis of research results presents five application areas of AIC in counseling studies, namely: (1) technology-based need assessment, (2) technology-based counseling process, (3) technology-based counseling media development, and (4) the ethical challenges of technology-based counseling applications. The implication is the need for further exploration of the ethical approach to technology and internet-based counseling application. © 2023 American Institute of Physics Inc.. All rights reserved.
