AB  - Drawing has always been a fundamental course in design education at the college and university level. With the advancement of technology, various emerging technologies have been introduced into teaching practices. In recent years, there has been significant attention given to the application of artificial intelligence (AI) technology, which has garnered admiration for its ability to produce remarkable images. This study aims to introduce new AI techniques for providing guidance and suggestions in drawing, with the goal of addressing the issues present in traditional computer graphics instruction. The study seeks to examine whether the new technology is capable of improving students' learning outcomes and fostering their interest in the subject. Data was collected through questionnaires administered to 52 game design students aged between 17 and 22 years old. Prior to the questionnaire survey, the students received instruction in computer drawing using AI image generation technology. Independent sample t-Tests were conducted to investigate the relationships between gender, prior experience with AI image generation technology, and various variables. However, no statistically significant correlations were observed. Additionally, exploratory factor analysis identified two correlated constructs: satisfaction and applicability. © 2023 IEEE.
