T2  - Lecture Notes in Networks and Systems
AB  - Be self-driving cars, multi-media recognition and processing, or content recommendation, Artificial Intelligence has wide range of applications in mitigating climate change, food shortage, defense equipment designing, cybersecurity, creating advance simulations supply chain, pollution, space exploration, genetic engineering, geology, and much more. Often termed as a bane, ethical AI is certainly impacting the world positively because of its uncontrolled potential. The ability to learn from past experiences enables machines and devices to perform tasks in complex, real-world situations, without constant user guidance. In this research, we propose a discussion on recent trends and advancements made in the field of Education. We deliver case studies of how Artificial intelligence and its sub-domains like Natural Language Processing, Computer Vision, and Machine Learning, along with sister technology like Augmented Reality and Virtual Reality, Cloud Computing, Brain Computing, IoT data processing, and Data Science are working hand in hand to provide significant up-gradation to the whole education sector. The research talks about Artificial intelligence’s impact on the teaching and administrative aspects of the education sector. We dive deep into the benefits generated on student’s and faculty’s sides while touching upon how Artificial intelligence has speeded up the administrative processes such as student selection, reports generation, resource planning, curriculum generation and analysis, and much more. © 2023, The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Switzerland AG.
