AB  - This chapter proposes several tools based on Artificial Intelligence (AI) and Augmented Reality (AR) to promote the transmission of knowledge in the educational context. AI is already used to provide assistance as part of educational processes (Squirrel AI, Google Classroom) and can generate effective methodological and assessment resources (Alexa, SIRI, NVIDIA Canvas, WriteToLearn, Lingvist, Duolingo, Gradescope, Smartick). In addition, the combination of AI and AR facilitates the learning of scientific, geographical, mathematical and social content through the use of interactive scenarios (Metaverse, Munzee, Goosechase, Blippar, PlugXr or ActionBound, Bodyplanet, Arloon Geometry, Chromville Science, Explore the World). The objectives of this chapter are to analyse the functionality, advantages and limitations of the use AI and AR in an educational environment, to illustrate its practical applicability and to create a table/guide with didactic examples. © 2023, The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Switzerland AG.
