T2  - Lecture Notes in Networks and Systems
AB  - The impact of artificial intelligence (AI) in its many forms such as machine learning, data mining, learning analytics, etc. is undeniable. It is transforming not only social and economic life, but also education. Thus, the chapter examines the influence of AI on teaching and learning in higher education. For this study, a scoping literature review was conducted to form a narrative overview of artificial intelligence in higher education. The synthesis of the results provides an assembly of key terminology such as machine learning, learning analytics, data mining, etc. as well as application in which these technologies are implemented such as for prediction, automation, etc. Often AI works in the background improving performances and offering advice or recommendations; thus, this pervasive technology becomes invisible to users. Overall, AI can contribute to a positive learning experience and motivation. Considering this digital transformation, competences and skills necessary for students and educators alike are shifting, so that so-called 21s century skills are gaining importance. © 2022, The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Switzerland AG.
