AB  - ”The National Contact Center (NCC) in the Kingdom of Bahrain,” the National Suggestion and Complaint network, is the communication channel in Bahrain for citizens and residents to express suggestions, questions, and complaints about all services provided by the government entities. Moreover, like any call center have its limitation and workload issues. This research develops a revolutionary, secured platform for an Intelligent Agent (IA) powered by Artificial Intelligent that conversationally engages with eGovernment customers. The designed platform uses Natural Language Processing (NLP) and deep learning (DL) to train the IA to understand questions and respond using Natural Language Generation (NLG). The platform is designed for the IA to respond directly to all received calls, answer questions, and take action by integrating to any call center system like Client Relationship Management (CRM) and directing requests to the appropriate area within the government. We designed the platform for a Bahraini IA who speaks two languages (Arabic and English) and has intelligent capabilities. The Intelligent agent Framework research is part of a comprehensive project proposed by us, and we are currently developing it with the Information and eGovernment Authority (iGA). This research includes project initiation and scoping, planning of project phases, and the architecture for the proposed solution. © 2021 IET Conference Proceedings. All rights reserved.
