TI  - Reimagining teacher development in the era of generative AI: A scoping review
AU  - Tan, Q.
T2  - Teaching and Teacher Education
AB  - Generative AI has great potential to revolutionize teacher development, yet reviews of its integration in this field remain limited. This scoping review analyzes 22 empirical studies, highlighting the underrepresentation of in-service teachers and small sample sizes, which raises concerns about bias. Key applications include resource development, personalized support, and creating learning environments, with intervention durations of 4–16 weeks. Seven outcomes were identified: improved learning, teacher knowledge, higher-order thinking, lesson design and implementation, self-worth and self-confidence, positive attitudes and usage intentions, and AI literacy. These insights can help design training programs to prepare teachers for effectively integrating generative AI. © 2025 Elsevier Ltd
