TI  - Prediction and Optimization Model for Ideological and Political Education Effectiveness in Universities Based on Deep Learning and Convolutional Neural Networks
AU  - Wang, Y.
AU  - Chen, L.
AB  - This paper proposes a deep learning-based prediction and optimization model for evaluating the effectiveness of ideological and political education (IPE) in universities. The model integrates a Multi-Scale Feature Convolutional Neural Network (MSF-CNN) with a Long Short-Term Memory (LSTM) architecture to extract and model multi-dimensional educational data, including behavioral sequences, emotional feedback, and classroom participation records. A customized optimization strategy is further embedded to convert predictive outputs into actionable teaching adjustments. Experimental evaluations on real-world datasets collected from multiple higher education institutions in Guangdong Province demonstrate that the proposed framework outperforms traditional machine learning models across all key metrics, including Accuracy, Precision, Recall, and F1-score. The system also shows substantial gains in classroom engagement, emotional stability, and academic performance after deployment. These results validate the technical viability and practical applicability of the proposed architecture in data-driven educational enhancement scenarios. © 2025 Copyright held by the owner/author(s).
