AU  - Khan, S.A.
AB  - The ever-increasing demand for sustainable practices in the tourism sector has placed green marketing as one of the concerns to promote environmentally friendly tourism behaviors. At the same time, artificial intelligence (AI) has become one of the most effective innovations empowering tourism marketing, providing means of personalisation, real-time decision making, and efficiency. This paper examines the interaction between the two fields-AI and green tourism marketing. By carrying out a detailed bibliometric analysis on 418 Scopus-indexed papers in the field, this study employs R Studio (Bibliometrix package) and VOSviewer to identify key contributors, trends and thematic development in influencing the field. The research has theoretical and practical implications because it revealed under studies concepts in the field of AI-supported sustainable tourism marketing. It postulates the need to pay more attention to ethical applications of AI, eco-personalization, and AI-powered plans that promote the Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs) in future research. © 2026, IGI Global Scientific Publishing.
