TI  - Enhancing the Implementation of Behavioural Insights in Education Using AI Tools
AU  - Lai, G.
AU  - Pheow, T.W.
AB  - This chapter explores how behavioural sciences can be applied to enhance the use of AI tools in education through the integration of behavioural insights (BI) and artificial intelligence (AI) as a synergistic approach to improving educational outcomes in higher education. From a behavioural lens, it argues that beyond classroom pedagogy, student success also hinges on behavioural, social, and emotional factors. Using BI frameworks and principles, educators can design effective “nudges” that positively influence student decision-making and engagement. With the advent of AI, conventional behavioural nudges can be further enhanced, giving rise to new frontiers of personalised digital nudges and learning environments. The chapter examines how AI technologies, particularly in natural language processing and learning analytics, can enhance the design of personalised nudges and behavioural solutions. The use of AI in delivering personalised digital nudges, chatbot-based interactions, and immersive life simulations offers scalable methods to foster students in both academic and non-academic outcomes. While the potential benefits are substantial, the chapter also addresses ethical concerns and calls for a thoughtful, human-centric integration of AI and BI, supported by robust ethical frameworks. The combined application of BI and AI promises to enhance teaching effectiveness, student outcomes, and learning environments—positioning education to better prepare students for both academic and lifelong success. © 2026 selection and editorial matter, Asha Kumaran, Boey Chee Kin, Cleta Milagros Acebedo, Gabrielle Lai, Linda William, Teo Chee Leng, Vijayan N, and Zhang Huiyu; individual chapters, the contributors.
