TI  - Enhancing Pronunciation and Grammar Learning in English Using a Multi-Task Learning with CNN-LSTM Hybrid-Based CALL System
AU  - Jerin Austin Dhas, J.
AU  - Rajab, A.B.
AU  - Deepika, P.
AU  - Thakre, N.K.
AU  - Alazzam, M.B.
AU  - Prema, S.
AB  - This research proposes a hybrid CNN-LSTM model based on a multi-task learning (MTL) approach to improve pronunciation and grammar training in computer-assisted language learning (CALL) systems. The CNN extracts meaningful acoustic features for pronunciation analysis, whereas the LSTM models sequential dependencies for correcting grammar. This hybrid approach is specifically adapted to process both temporal speech patterns and syntactic structures concomitantly. A multilingual dataset consisting of 2,140 speakers from 177 countries and 214 native languages was employed. The model surpasses baseline Transformer and LSTM-only models with a BLEU score of 0.85, 91.7% grammar accuracy, and 89.5% sentence fluency. Pronunciation evaluation measures are 90.1% phoneme classification accuracy, 88.9% pronunciation score per word, and 87.6% fluency score. A common MTL loss function allows the model to give reliable real-time feedback on both tasks. The outcomes illustrate the competence of the model and the practical utility of deep learning-based CALL tools for international language learners. © 2025 IEEE.
