AB  - Higher education is undergoing rapid transformation, driven by advancements in artificial intelligence (AI) and big data (BD) analytics. This research explores how AI and BD analytics can work together to assess and enhance the quality of university education. Employing a questionnaire-based approach, data were gathered from 420 students and 118 teachers, with analysis conducted using SPSS software to derive meaningful insights. The results reveal that integrating AI and BD analytics in UE administration enhances resource allocation efficiency, leading to cost reductions and heightened operational effectiveness. This research pioneers the integration of AI and BD analytics for a comprehensive evaluation of UE quality, providing valuable insights and practical recommendations to drive ongoing improvement and foster innovation in HE. The study emphasizes the significant impact of AI technologies in transforming the landscape of university education, emphasizing improvements in student retention, personalized learning, engagement, resource allocation efficiency, assessment validity, and academic integrity. Additionally, it showcases the positive outcomes of AI-driven recommendation systems in student course selection and academic advising, leading to increased student engagement and proactive academic planning. © 2025 Informa UK Limited, trading as Taylor & Francis Group.
