AB  - Schools, teachers, and students have long dreamed about personalized learning, nevertheless until lately, educators lacked the time and means to put it into practice on a wide scale. Thanks to AI breakthroughs, many of a teacher's routine responsibilities, like producing lesson resources, can now be automated with generative AI. making slideshows, infographics, and lesson plans; translating text into pictures and videos; and producing infographics. The creation and assessment of an AI-powered tutoring system intended to improve student learning experiences are described in depth in this paper. Driven by the promise of artificial intelligence (AI) to revolutionize the field of education, the project endeavors to leverage big language models, such as OpenAI, to establish a customized and flexible learning environment. The investigation is conducted in two phases: the first is the research phase, which includes a thorough literature review, problem definition, and AI integration; the subsequent stage is the design and development phase, which includes prototyping, testing, and design. Using the GPT-3.5-Turbo paradigm, the course production procedure highlights the cooperative efforts of AI algorithms and human tutors. The study found that using text-to-voice, an automatic speech recognition system from Whisper, to create courses that use AI has the possibility of helping strengthen education. © 2025 Author(s).
