TI  - Artificial intelligence in education and changing teacher roles
AU  - Atasoy, R.
AB  - This book chapter aims to present a holistic and innovative perspective on AI in education and its impact on evolving teacher roles. It seeks to raise awareness of AI- enabled teaching practices while offering a transformative framework to enhance teachers' professional development and promote sustainable education. Additionally, this chapter provides both theoretical and practical insights into the shifting needs of educators as they navigate the transition from today's complex educational landscape to AI- integrated learning environments, which have the potential to shape future educational paradigms. In line with these objectives, the chapter explores various perspectives on integrating AI to support teacher development, reframe teacher leadership, and equip school administrators and policymakers with a comprehensive understanding of AI's opportunities and challenges in education. Furthermore, it examines how AI enhances education, fosters professional development, and improves student outcomes while addressing potential risks and ethical considerations. © 2025, IGI Global Scientific Publishing. All rights reserved.
