AU  - Singh, B.
AB  - The healthcare landscape is undergoing a revolutionary shift, driven by the relentless march of digital transformation. There are emerging technologies like Augmented Reality (AR) and Virtual Reality (VR) poised to reshape how it delivers and experience healthcare across the globe. AR superimposes digital information onto the real world, offering real-time guidance and visualization during medical procedures. Imagine surgeons viewing 3D anatomical models overlaid on a patient during surgery, or dentists using AR- powered apps to guide dental implant placement with precision. VR immerses users in simulated environments, enabling applications like phobia therapy, pain management and even surgical training in highly realistic scenarios. The true potential of AR and VR unfolds when woven into the fabric of smart healthcare ecosystems. This chapter dives into the exciting possibilities these technologies offer, exploring their integration into smart healthcare ecosystems and the creation of transformative health gateways within a global context. © 2025, IGI Global Scientific Publishing. All rights reserved.
