TI  - Mapping the evolution of generative AI: insights from bibliometric research
AU  - Pathak, S.
AU  - Pallasena, R.K.
T2  - Journal of Decision Systems
AB  - Generative Artificial Intelligence (Gen-AI) marks a pivotal milestone in the capabilities of machine and Artificial Intelligence (AI) to create new content, designs, and solutions autonomously. While there has been a notable surge on Gen-AI research recently, comprehensive systematic reviews remain limited. Motivated by the rising investments, and excitement due to its potential, we present a state-of-the-art bibliometric review of Gen-AI research, utilising 5346 scholarly articles between 2015 and 2024. The study employs several methods such as citation, co-citation and centrality analysis to uncover the field’s intellectual core. We also trace the development and maturity of the field by applying Lotka’s law, Bradford law, and critical research milestones. The study reveals four core themes from the review which relate to (a) Advancements in Gen-AI Architecture and Frameworks, (b) Gen-AI Applications, (c) Model Validation and Benchmarking, (d) Systemic Considerations. The paper recommends several actionable future research directions, and testable research propositions under each theme. © 2024 Informa UK Limited, trading as Taylor & Francis Group.
