TI  - The Convergence of Generative AI and Ethical Consideration
AU  - Sunkara, A.
AU  - Pravalika, A.
AU  - Patnaik, P.
AB  - In the field of generative artificial intelligence (AI), ethical considerations are crucial since they have a big impact on the responsible development, use, and advancement of AI-powered technology. This book chapter explores the complicated ethical landscape surrounding generative AI, looking at guiding principles, roadblocks, and suggested frameworks that can help with ethical application and discussion. The chapter begins with a thorough analysis of the ethical considerations that are fundamental to generative AI. From there, it delves into specific areas of concern, including data control and scraping, data privacy and security, accountability, and authenticity, as well as bias reduction, fairness procedures, data usage transparency, and technology perceptions. Each section of this paper analyses the moral implications, challenges, and best practices associated with these topics, drawing insights from research studies, real-world experiences, and case studies. Furthermore, the chapter lays forth a suggested ethical framework that integrates principles of responsibility, security, openness, equity, privacy, human-centred design, and ethical impact assessment to direct the responsible advancement and application of artificial intelligence. Through a thorough examination of the ethical landscape, this chapter seeks to improve understanding of the ethical implications of generative AI and foster an atmosphere that prioritises transparency, integrity, and moral progress in AI-driven endeavours. © 2025 selection and editorial matter, Raul V. Rodriguez and Hemachandran K.
