AB  - This chapter discusses the role of artificial intelligence (AI) in preserving and revitalizing endangered languages. Amidst language decline caused by globalization, urbanization, and the dominance of international languages, AI is developing technologies with documentation approaches (e.g., creation of machine translation, audio recordings, written texts, and linguistic analyses) and collaboration (applications for joint activities). Despite challenges such as data scarcity and ethical issues related to indigenous knowledge, successful cases, such as the revitalization of Hawaiian and Maori, highlight the potential of AI to combat language extinction. This chapter provides valuable insights for linguists, researchers, and policymakers who advocate for interdisciplinary collaboration and the development of ethical AI that respects and preserves the rights of indigenous peoples. © 2026 by IGI Global Scientific Publishing. All rights reserved.
