AU  - Kaunert, C.
AB  - Healthcare is undergoing a shift towards a proactive approach as outlined in the P5 medicine concept which emphasizes predictiveness, personalization, prevention, participation and precision in healthcare practices. This patient-centric model heavily relies on advanced technologies like artificial intelligence (AI) and robotics to enhance the processes of diagnosis, decision-making and treatment. The narrative then shifts to the progress in understanding the human body at various levels, including molecular and sub-molecular levels, leading to a deeper comprehension of diseases. AI and robotics are portrayed as crucial tools leveraging knowledge and patient data for tasks such as diagnosis, surgery planning, and monitoring patient well-being. This chapter explores the role of AI and robotic systems in this transformation, providing examples of their applications. The systems are categorized based on various factors such as their type, level of autonomy, the care settings they are utilized in and their application areas. © 2026 Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.
