AB  - Chapter 4 describes a responsive instructional design approach embedding generative artificial intelligence (GenAI) in the context of teaching and learning in post-secondary settings. Responsive instructors understand the interconnection of the components in a learning system and make purposeful changes to their learning designs. The authors use a Digital Skill Development Framework to describe their responsive approach for designing online courses. Intersections with experiential learning and open education practices underscore their approaches for developing technology-mediated learning designs. The framework used holds promise for planning courses or lessons using GenAI-powered tools and conducting future research in instructional design. © The Editor and Contributing Authors Severally 2025.
