AB  - Fusing AI into education, has impelled the requisite to reconnoiter its magnitude, acuity, and outcome as an academic furtherance tool. This enquiry probe to fathom the AI readiness and interconnectedness of perceived usefulness, (AI for social good, AI in the educational sphere). Inferences on the AI readiness and behavioral intention of learners and indulgent if there are moderating roles of (gender, habit, confidence) in using AI to enhance learning. A Partial Least Squares Structural Equation Modeling (PLS-SEM) analysis was employed grounded on the 604 (Ramon V. Del Rosario, College of Business, De La Salle University) respondents using a convenience sampling approach. Outcomes denote that (attitude, confidence, relevance) in using AI positively influences behavioral intention. Moreover, AI for (social good, confidence and relevance) unequivocally influences AI readiness. AI alacrity mediates the relationship of different variables with behavioral intention. The probe acmes the need to enrich an AI-ready acculturation amidst tailored training programs and curricular innovation, underlining ethical and sensible AI use. Yonder the distinctive institutional context, these outcomes enrich global theoretical frameworks by parading the multifarious interplay of psychological, cultural, and educational dynamics in fostering AI readiness. This delves into stratagems for integrating AI into education logics worldwide, paving the way for comprehensive and impactful AI espousal in diverse learning environs. © 2025 GMP Press and Printing.
