AB  - Artificial intelligence is increasing its pace and is getting enormous scope. Generative AI has brought new hope to disruption in different industries and made sharper and more realistic virtual content. Generative AI models and systems are progressing significantly and are now offered massively across a wide range of industries and applications. The product of advancement in this area will be writing and email AI assistants, graphic design and art production, creatively exceptional AI tutoring associates, programming, and medicine. This chapter presents innovative developments, in particular, bringing forth a lot of ethical issues that must be taken seriously so that the implementation of AI systems will be carried out in the right way. The study delves further into the ethical dilemmas that arise in the software engineering domain. This chapter has proved that ethical analysis cannot be underrated; thus appropriate measures and controls are necessary for tackling the AI ethics problems of the future. © 2026 selection and editorial matter Rajendra Kumar, Shankar Ramamoorthy, Vishal Jain, Utku Köse and Ong Eng Tek; individual chapters, the contributors.
