AU  - Hadidi, A.
AB  - Several innovations related to generative artificial intelligence (GAI) applications emerged in the direction of new, revolutionary healthcare solutions. The chapter presents an overview of the current state of GAI applications in healthcare and is focused on analyzing its probable development perspectives. There is a wide spectrum of applications that GAI embraces currently, including medical image analysis, drug discovery, patient diagnostics, and personalized treatment planning. Generative model–powered algorithms have indeed been very impressive in image recognition as anomalies are detected with high accuracy and thus would assist in early disease diagnosis. GAI has also greatly found an application in drug discovery processes, forecasting possible candidates for drugs and the optimization of molecular structures. The pertinent challenges remain data privacy, ethical considerations, and a need for standard regulatory frameworks. The author elaborates on these challenges and postulates strategies for their address with regard to the responsible and ethical deployment of GAI in healthcare. Such integration of AI-driven technologies into clinical workflows potentially enhances diagnostic accuracy, improves treatment outcomes, and lowers healthcare costs. Finally, GAI can be combined with current next-generation technologies, such as blockchain and IoMT, to transform how data is shared, interoperated on, and securely managed in the health record. © 2026 selection and editorial matter Rajendra Kumar, Shankar Ramamoorthy, Vishal Jain, Utku Köse and Ong Eng Tek; individual chapters, the contributors.
