TI  - BUILDING TEACHER CAPACITY FOR EFFECTIVE INTEGRATION OF GENAI INTO CLASSROOM: A Framework for Teacher Education Programs
AU  - Nair, H.B.
AB  - This chapter presents a comprehensive framework for building teacher capacity to effectively integrate Generative Artificial Intelligence (GenAI) into educational settings. It begins by exploring the transformative potential of GenAI, emphasizing its ability to personalize learning, create educational materials, and support teachers. The literature review highlights the impact of GenAI on education and identifies the challenges and needs of teachers in adopting this technology. The proposed framework includes an eight-week course design targeted at K-12 educators, structured around the TPACK framework and social learning theory. The course is divided into three modules: “Demystifying GenAI,” “Unleashing Learning with GenAI,” and “Assessment and the Evolving GenAI Classroom,” each focusing on the specific aspects of GenAI integration. The chapter underscores the importance of GenAI literacy, ethical considerations, and pedagogical strategies in teacher training programs. By equipping educators with the necessary skills and knowledge, the framework aims to enhance the teaching and learning outcomes, ultimately fostering a more innovative and effective educational environment. © 2025 selection and editorial matter, Mahmoud Elkhodr and Ergun Gide.
