TY  - CHAP
TI  - IMPACT OF GENAI ON STUDENT OUTCOMES
AU  - Divya, G.S.
AB  - The integration of artificial intelligence (AI) into education has revolutionized traditional teaching and learning methods. Among AI’s various applications in education, Generative Artificial Intelligence (GenAI)-empowered learning stands out as a significant advancement. GenAI leverages GenAI algorithms to create immersive, personalized, and adaptive learning experiences for students. This chapter explores the evolution of AI and GenAI, tracing key developments from the 1950s to the 2020s, highlighting breakthroughs such as machine learning, deep learning, generative adversarial networks (GANs), and natural language processing (NLP). The introduction of ChatGPT in 2022 exemplifies the rapid adoption and potential of AI in education, offering personalized learning and formative assessment support, albeit with concerns about accuracy, privacy, and academic integrity. GenAI’s ability to generate novel data, such as text and images, promises to transform learning, instruction, and content creation, tailoring educational experiences to individual student needs. It enhances engagement through interactive simulations, multimedia content, and adaptive learning trajectories, fostering creativity, collaboration, and critical 21st century skills. Despite its benefits, the implementation of GenAI necessitates careful consideration of ethical, privacy, and equity issues to ensure fair access to high-quality education. This chapter also examines the challenges and strategies associated with integrating ChatGPT and similar AI tools into educational settings, emphasizing the importance of collaboration among stakeholders. © 2025 selection and editorial matter, Mahmoud Elkhodr and Ergun Gide.
