TI  - Unlocking learners’ potential in English language learning: the synergy of artificial intelligence, cognitive science, and ChatGPT
AU  - Giray, L.
T2  - Learning: Research and Practice
AB  - Despite the growing enthusiasm for ChatGPT in classrooms, many teachers still approach its use without a clear, structured framework. This paper contends that to truly harness its potential, ChatGPT must be employed with intentionality, guided by research-backed cognitive science strategies. It outlines ten cognitive strategies and practical examples to help learners get the most out of ChatGPT as a strategic tool for mastering English. When used in this way, ChatGPT becomes a personalized tutor that may offer a solution to Bloom’s two-sigma problem. It enables learners to progress at their own pace, identify cognitive strengths and areas for improvement, and take greater ownership of their learning. This intentional use of AI shifts language learning from passive engagement, often linked to superficial understanding, to an active, deeply engaging process that reinforces long-term mastery. Moreover, AI, like ChatGPT, has the potential to amplify human capabilities by embedding cognitive science principles into everyday learning. Beyond enhancing language acquisition, it nurtures higher-order thinking and adaptability. It transforms the learning experience into one that not only supports academic success but also fosters lifelong intellectual growth. However, ChatGPT is not a panacea. Its limitations, including occasional inaccuracies and a lack of nuanced feedback, call for a balanced approach. By integrating ChatGPT with traditional language learning methods, such as face-to-face practice and real-world interaction, teachers may create a more holistic and effective educational environment. © 2025 Informa UK Limited, trading as Taylor & Francis Group.
