AU  - Kerem, K.
AB  - Academics often face time constraints, limiting engagement in essential, longer-term tasks. This chapter explores ChatGPT’s potential in higher education, highlighting its practical applications from course planning to student-centred learning. Unique features such as ease of access, personalized responses, and cost-effectiveness make ChatGPT an ideal “virtual colleague”. It aids in course design, developing learning outcomes and supporting constructivist learning by encouraging active student participation and tailoring content to local contexts. The guidance provided highlights how ChatGPT can alleviate workload pressures, addressing the time constraints faced by academics. However, it underscores the necessity of validating AI outputs to ensure accuracy and maintain the essential human elements of education. Detailed examples and strategies offer a balanced perspective on leveraging AI to complement human intelligence and enhance academic productivity, providing a comprehensive overview of integrating generative AI into higher education to support educators in their instructional processes. © The Editors and Contributing Authors Severally 2025. All rights reserved.
