T2  - Journal of Further and Higher Education
AB  - To gain a deeper understanding of the developmental trends and hotspots in research on learning interest. By using the bibliometric analysis method, we analysed the citation network and co-occurrence network of papers on learning interest published from 2014 to 2024. The analysis focused on various aspects, including temporal trends, publishing journals, countries, institutions, and research hotspots, resulting in the construction of a knowledge graph. The findings reveal a recent decline in the annual number of publications. The journal Research in Science Education has the highest number of publications, while the United States leads in the total number of articles. Among institutions, the University of Helsinki stands out as the most prolific contributor to research on learning interest. The primary research topics include STEM education, situational interest, academic self-concept, mathematics self-efficacy, interest development, and teacher care. Finally, we propose some measures to promote student interest to assist educators. © 2025 UCU.
