TY  - CHAP
TI  - Multimodal GAI in arts-based multiliteracies: Fostering interdisciplinary creativity
AU  - Hutson, J.
AB  - This chapter proposes an innovative integration of multimodal generative artificial intelligence (GAI) interfaces within the framework of arts-based multiliteracies. It argues for the indispensability of such integration in dismantling traditional hierarchies that prioritize reading and writing over other semiotic systems. The chapter elucidates how leveraging GAI interfaces in education reinforces the significance of arts-based semiotic sign systems, thereby challenging the longstanding supremacy of text-centric literacies. It further demonstrates how these advanced technological tools can facilitate interdisciplinary educational strategies across fine and performing arts, enabling a seamless appreciation and engagement with various art forms. This approach effectively removes creative barriers, encouraging cross-disciplinary pollination previously hindered by the compartmentalization of artistic disciplines. © 2025 by IGI Global. All rights reserved.
