TI  - Global perspectives on personalized learning: Case studies and best practices
AU  - Kayyali, M.
AB  - This chapter presents a comprehensive investigation of individualised learning from a global perspective, including a variety of case studies and best practices from varied educational contexts around the world. As education undergoes a major transition in reaction to technological breakthroughs and evolving pedagogical approaches, the concept of individualised learning has acquired great support. This chapter delves into the numerous methods in which personalized learning is implemented, adapted, and perfected across different cultural, social, and educational contexts. Through an assessment of real-world case studies, readers get insights into effective methods, obstacles, and innovative solutions applied in personalized learning efforts. By stressing the transnational elements of customised learning, this chapter adds to a fuller understanding of its potential and adaptability, promoting the exchange of ideas and practices on a global scale. © 2024, IGI Global. All rights reserved.
