TI  - Innovation of Teaching Methods of Civic and Political Education in Colleges and Universities with the Assistance of Artificial Intelligence
AU  - Lv, H.
T2  - Applied Mathematics and Nonlinear Sciences
AB  - Artificial intelligence empowers education and promotes its integration and innovation, enabling the use of learning analytics to accurately diagnose the learning situation and implement precise teaching. In this paper, we have leveraged artificial intelligence to innovate traditional teaching methods, developed a wisdom teaching model specifically for college civic education, and concentrated on the precise application of wisdom teaching in this context. First, it creates student profiles based on academic data and then provides personalized recommendations for learning resources by combining a collaborative filtering algorithm and an improved K-means algorithm. Finally, we analyze the actual impact of the teaching intervention by comparing the student portraits before and after the intervention. When the number of neighbors K takes the same value, the improved cosine similarity calculation method outperforms other calculation methods, and the RMSE, MAE, accuracy, recall, and F1 values are 0.14, 0.24, 0.99, 0.74, and 0.85 when K = 60, respectively, which indicates that the algorithm improvement in this paper is practical. This paper categorizes the sample students into four groups based on their learning behavior and outcomes: potential, excellent, marginal, and hardworking. All these student types have demonstrated some progress following the teaching intervention, confirming the efficacy of this paper's artificial intelligence-based teaching approach for college civic education. Simultaneously, the created profiles of these student types establish the groundwork for future personalized and accurate instruction. © 2024 Huan Lv, published by Sciendo.
