AB  - Digital transformation involves using digital technologies to benefit society and the healthcare industry. Healthcare systems must adopt digital technology to develop innovative solutions for enhancing healthcare delivery and addressing medical issues. This transformation encompasses changes related to the internet, digital technologies, and their integration with new therapies and best practices for better health management. Managing the quality of massive data collected can improve patient well- being and reduce service costs. Also, digital technologies will influence medical education, leading experts to devise new training methods. Consequently, practitioners will encounter new opportunities in their field. This chapter focuses on the digital transformation of healthcare with a particular focus on the integration of Augmented Reality (AR) and Virtual Reality (VR) technologies are redefining healthcare delivery, training and patient interaction on a global scale. © 2025 by IGI Global Scientific Publishing.
