AB  - This paper aims at filling this gap through dissecting the applicability of the Generative AI in the current learning and teaching system. The paper offers an introduction to Generative AI technologies: GPT and DALL-E, and describes the chronological history and current progress of its educational applications. Other objectives include discussing about the uses of Generative AI in adaptive learning environment, smart learning systems, automation of organizational work and in talented minds improvement. Analyzing key successful AI cases, the paper reveals the challenges implementers encountered, and provides debates about the appropriate practices of AI. Research evidence points to the prospect of Generative AI benefiting students and educators in teaching and learning, which indicates the innovative potential of the technology, yet at the same time reveals the potential risks and challenges that need to be addressed concerning the ethical and privacy implications of Generative AI in education. Others may follow general recommendations for policymakers and educators on how to integrate artificial intelligence responsibly, as well as future work for this quickly burgeoning domain. © 2024 IEEE.
