AB  - The integration of Artificial Intelligence (AI) into English language teaching (ELT) has transformed academic practices by means of enhancing personalization, interactivity, and engagement. Traditional teaching techniques often conflict to provide individualized mastering experiences and timely feedback, main to varied pupil results and engagement degrees. Despite the provision of digital equipment, many current techniques lack the sophistication wished for adaptive learning and real-time interplay, ensuing in limited personalization and inconsistent academic help. This study introduces a comprehensive evaluation of AI's impact on ELT environments, focusing on personalized mastering paths, interactive remarks, and gamification. The novelty of the proposed technique lies in its mixed-techniques design, combining quantitative surveys, qualitative interviews, and case studies to assess AI equipment' effectiveness comprehensively. The study assesses adaptive gaining knowledge of systems, intelligent tutoring systems, and gamified structures to perceive their benefits and obstacles. The typical technique includes a literature assessment to contextualize AI advancements in schooling, followed with the aid of surveys to collect quantitative information on AI tool utilization and effectiveness amongst educators and college students. Semi-established interviews offer in-intensity qualitative insights, whilst case studies provide realistic examples of AI implementation in real-international settings. Data evaluation employs statistical strategies for quantitative outcomes and thematic analysis for qualitative records, integrating findings to give a holistic view of AI's impact. Results indicate that AI notably complements personalized getting to know and engagement but also famous challenges such as data privacy concerns and ranging effectiveness throughout exceptional tools. © 2024 IEEE.
