AB  - Technological tools have been increasingly incorporated into education through the last decades, and haptic devices' irruption in 2010 has disrupted how children learn nowadays. These devices have accompanied the youngsters born since then who got used to getting any piece of information of their interest at any time and from any place in whatever setting just using haptic gestures on them. With their use, they even learn unconsciously in informal and non-formal settings. In this paper, we recall recent advances that lead to suggest that higher education institutions should transform and boost smart learning so that this cohort keeps acquiring deep knowledge in what has become natural for them, learning with an Active attitude, which aligns with Peace Engineering educational focus on paying attention to the needs of the most vulnerable populations by equipping communities with the right knowledge, at the right place, at the right time. © 2023 IEEE.
